{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788236729288,"sessionID":"ses_fa4ccfc0bffexSFu2vIRQjobrF","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_2e91e306b510427d80cc581f","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"./venv/bin/python << 'EOF'\nimport csv, collections, unicodedata, re\n\ndef base_state(name):\n    name = re.sub(r'\\(.*?\\)', ' ', name)\n    m = re.search(r'\\s*-\\s*([A-Z]{2})\\s*$', name.strip())\n    state = None\n    if m:\n        state = m.group(1); name = name[:m.start()]\n    nk = unicodedata.normalize('NFKD', name)\n    b = ''.join(c for c in nk if not unicodedata.combining(c)).strip().lower()\n    return b, state\n\npairs = collections.Counter()\ndef scan(path, cols):\n    with open(path, encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        for row in csv.DictReader(f):\n            for c in cols:\n                if c in row and row[c]:\n                    b, s = base_state(row[c])\n                    pairs[(b, s)] += 1\n\nscan('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv', ['home_team'])\nscan('data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv', ['home_team'])\nscan('data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv', ['home_team'])\nscan('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv', ['home'])\nscan('data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv', ['Equipe_mandante'])\n\n# find base names with multiple states\nbybase = collections.defaultdict(set)\nfor (b, s), n in pairs.items():\n    if s: bybase[b].add(s)\ncoll = {b: sorted(s) for b, s in bybase.items() if len(s) > 1}\nprint('Base-name collisions:', coll)\nprint()\n# bases WITHOUT state (need checking)\nnostate = {b: n for (b,s),n in pairs.items() if s is None and n > 5}\nprint('No-state names (top):', dict(sorted(nostate.items(), key=lambda kv:-kv[1])[:25]))\nEOF"},"output":"Base-name collisions: {'botafogo': ['PB', 'RJ'], 'internacional': ['RS', 'SC'], 'atletico': ['AC', 'BA', 'ES', 'GO', 'MG', 'PR'], 'flamengo': ['PI', 'RJ'], 'nautico': ['PE', 'RR'], 'santos': ['AP', 'SP'], 'santa cruz': ['PE', 'RN', 'RS'], 'america': ['MG', 'RN'], 'juventude': ['MA', 'RS'], 'guarani': ['CE', 'SP'], 'comercial': ['MS', 'PI'], 'rio branco': ['AC', 'ES'], 'sao raimundo': ['PA', 'RR'], 'bragantino': ['PA', 'SP'], 'operario': ['MS', 'MT', 'PR'], 'ypiranga': ['AP', 'RS']}\n\nNo-state names (top): {'flamengo': 584, 'cruzeiro': 567, 'sao paulo': 566, 'santos': 562, 'gremio': 560, 'fluminense': 551, 'corinthians': 548, 'palmeiras': 541, 'internacional': 535, 'goias': 439, 'coritiba': 431, 'figueirense': 384, 'vitoria': 382, 'ponte preta': 381, 'avai': 311, 'chapecoense': 309, 'ceara': 280, 'vasco': 279, 'parana': 270, 'criciuma': 261, 'paysandu': 217, 'atletico mineiro': 210, 'botafogo rj': 208, 'vasco da gama rj': 205, 'ec bahia': 203}\n","metadata":{"output":"Base-name collisions: {'botafogo': ['PB', 'RJ'], 'internacional': ['RS', 'SC'], 'atletico': ['AC', 'BA', 'ES', 'GO', 'MG', 'PR'], 'flamengo': ['PI', 'RJ'], 'nautico': ['PE', 'RR'], 'santos': ['AP', 'SP'], 'santa cruz': ['PE', 'RN', 'RS'], 'america': ['MG', 'RN'], 'juventude': ['MA', 'RS'], 'guarani': ['CE', 'SP'], 'comercial': ['MS', 'PI'], 'rio branco': ['AC', 'ES'], 'sao raimundo': ['PA', 'RR'], 'bragantino': ['PA', 'SP'], 'operario': ['MS', 'MT', 'PR'], 'ypiranga': ['AP', 'RS']}\n\nNo-state names (top): {'flamengo': 584, 'cruzeiro': 567, 'sao paulo': 566, 'santos': 562, 'gremio': 560, 'fluminense': 551, 'corinthians': 548, 'palmeiras': 541, 'internacional': 535, 'goias': 439, 'coritiba': 431, 'figueirense': 384, 'vitoria': 382, 'ponte preta': 381, 'avai': 311, 'chapecoense': 309, 'ceara': 280, 'vasco': 279, 'parana': 270, 'criciuma': 261, 'paysandu': 217, 'atletico mineiro': 210, 'botafogo rj': 208, 'vasco da gama rj': 205, 'ec bahia': 203}\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"./venv/bin/python << 'EOF'\nimport csv, collections, unicodedata, re\n\ndef base_state(name):\n    name = re.sub(r'\\(.*?\\)', ' ', name)\n    m = re.search(r'\\s*-\\s*([A-Z]{2})\\s*$', name.strip())\n    state = None\n    if m:\n        state = m.group(1); name = name[:m.start()]\n    nk = unicodedata.normalize('NFKD', name)\n    b = ''.join(c for c in nk if not unicodedata.combining(c)).strip().lower()\n    return b, state\n\npairs = collections.Counter()\ndef scan(path, cols):\n    with open(path, encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        for row in csv.DictReader(f):\n            for c in cols:\n                if c in row and row[c]:\n                    b, s = base_state(row[c])\n                    pairs[(b, s)] += 1\n\nscan('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv', ['home_team'])\nscan('data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv', ['home_team'])\nscan('data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv', ['home_team'])\nscan('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv', ['home'])\nscan('data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv', ['Equipe_mandante'])\n\n# find base names with multiple states\nbybase = collections.defaultdict(set)\nfor (b, s), n in pairs.items():\n    if s: bybase[b].add(s)\ncoll = {b: sorted(s) for b, s in bybase.items() if len(s) > 1}\nprint('Base-name collisions:', coll)\nprint()\n# bases WITHOUT state (need checking)\nnostate = {b: n for (b,s),n in pairs.items() if s is None and n > 5}\nprint('No-state names (top):', dict(sorted(nostate.items(), key=lambda kv:-kv[1])[:25]))\nEOF","time":{"start":1788236729284,"end":1788236729287}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Interesting! The \"atletico: 112 pts\" is wrong — it merged atletico-MG and atletico-PR into \"atletico\" because my quick norm strips state suffix \"-PR\"/\"-MG\"?? No wait, it strips \"-SP\" style suffix but \"Atletico-MG\" → strips \"-MG\" → \"atletico\". Right — both Atletico-MG and Atletico-PR become \"atletico\"! That's exactly the team-name normalization challenge: I can NOT blindly strip the state suffix because \"Atlético-MG\" and \"Atlético-PR\" are DIFFERENT clubs whose base names are both \"Atlético\".\n\nSo normalization needs club identity resolution, not just suffix stripping. The state suffix is actually part of the club identity when base names collide!\n\nCorrect approach: build an alias/identity table mapping all name variants to a canonical club ID. Known collisions:\n- Atletico-MG / Atletico Mineiro / Atlético-MG → \"Atlético Mineiro\" (MG)\n- Atletico-PR / Athletico-PR / Athletico Paranaense / Atlético-PR / Atletico Paranaense → \"Athletico Paranaense\" (PR)\n- Atletico-GO / Atletico Goianiense / Atlético-GO → \"Atlético Goianiense\" (GO)\n- America-MG / América-MG / America MG → \"América Mineiro\"\n- America-RN / América-RN → \"América (RN)\" — different club from America-MG!\n- Botafogo-RJ / Botafogo RJ vs Botafogo-SP / Botafogo SP → different clubs!\n- Sport-PE / Sport Recife → \"Sport Recife\"\n- Vitoria-BA vs Vitoria-ES(?) → Vitória (BA); Rio Branco? careful.\n\nSo the rule: normalization keeps the state suffix as part of the identity when the base name is ambiguous. Better: canonical identity = \"base + state\" when state known. E.g.:\n- \"Atletico-MG\" → id \"atletico-mg\"; \"Atletico Mineiro\" (BRFB) → needs alias to \"atletico-mg\". BRFB also has \"Atletico Goianiense\", \"Athletico Paranaense\", \"Atletico Mineiro\" — full names that disambiguate naturally.\n- Hist file: 'Atlético-MG' with state in separate column Mandante_UF. So hist \"Atlético-MG\"... wait hist home names shown: 'América-MG', 'Athletico-PR', 'Atlético-GO', 'Atlético-MG' — they include suffix. And also has separate UF columns. OK.\n\nSo canonicalization algorithm:\n1. Extract base name and state: from suffix \"-XX\" pattern or from separate UF column when available.\n2. Unaccent, lowercase base.\n3. Alias mapping for full names: \"atletico mineiro\" → base \"atletico\", state \"mg\"; \"athletico paranaense\"/\"atletico paranaense\" → \"atletico-pr\"; \"atletico goianiense\" → \"atletico-go\"; \"america mineiro\" → \"america-mg\"; \"botafogo rj\"?? BRFB has \"Botafogo RJ\" and \"Botafogo SP\" — with states. Good.\n4. Key = base if no collision else base+state.\n\nCollisions among real club base names (in Brazilian soccer): atletico (MG/PR/GO), america (MG/RN), botafogo (RJ/SP), vitoria (BA, and maybe ES), internacional vs inter? \"Internacional\" vs \"Inter de Limeira\"? In Série B/C there are: \"Inter de Limeira\"? BRFB Serie C might have. Also \"Rio Branco\"? Let me scan all distinct team base names across all files and find collisions.\n\nThen canonical display names: \"Atlético Mineiro\" etc. For simplicity, canonical ID = normalized \"base-state\" (e.g. \"atletico-mg\"), display = the most common original variant or a curated display map for famous clubs.\n\nFor user queries: resolve_team(\"Atlético-MG\") → exact; resolve_team(\"Atletico Mineiro\") → alias; resolve_team(\"Palmeiras\") → \"palmeiras\". Also handle \"São Paulo FC\" from FIFA → \"sao paulo\".\n\nAlso FIFA club names: \"Flamengo\", \"Palmeiras\", \"São Paulo\"? FIFA 19 Brazilian clubs: Palmeiras, Flamengo, São Paulo, Santos, Grêmio, Corinthians? (Corinthians not in FIFA 19 — they signed with Konami/PES! Indeed FIFA 19 lacks Corinthians; Brazilian clubs in FIFA 19 are limited: Palmeiras, Flamengo, São Paulo, Santos, Grêmio, Athletico Paranaense? Actually FIFA 19 had Brazilian league with generic players? The dataset has 18k players... FIFA 19 full dataset includes Brazilian clubs but Corinthians/Flamengo? Let me just check quickly which Brazilian clubs appear in fifa_data.csv.)\n\nLet me now scan for base-name collisions and FIFA Brazilian clubs. Then finalize the design and write code.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b370b540014SLCXd4Z93vHQy","sessionID":"ses_fa4ccfc0bffexSFu2vIRQjobrF","messageID":"msg_05b3670a4001qmNe6iqD1JkzAo"}}
