{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788236798001,"sessionID":"ses_fa4ccfc0bffexSFu2vIRQjobrF","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_b3792001b28c40a7bc7b89b9","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"./venv/bin/python << 'EOF'\nimport csv, collections, unicodedata, re\n\ndef unaccent(s):\n    return ''.join(c for c in unicodedata.normalize('NFKD', s) if not unicodedata.combining(c))\n\n# FIFA Brazilian clubs (clubs that look Brazilian)\nwith open('data/kaggle/fifa_data.csv', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    clubs = collections.Counter(row['Club'] for row in csv.DictReader(f))\nbrazilian = ['Flamengo','Palmeiras','São Paulo','Santos','Grêmio','Corinthians','Athletico','Atlético','Mineiro','Paranaense','Bahia','Vasco','Botafogo','Cruzeiro','Fluminense','Internacional','Goiás','Sport','Chapecoense','Ceará','Fortaleza','América','Avaí','Criciúma','Paysandu','Goiás','Coritiba','Vitória','Bahia','Athletic']\nhits = {c: n for c, n in clubs.items() if any(b.lower() in unaccent(c).lower() for b in brazilian)}\nprint('FIFA BR clubs:', hits)\nEOF"},"output":"FIFA BR clubs: {'Sporting CP': 30, 'Atlético Mineiro': 20, 'Cruzeiro': 20, 'Athletic Club de Bilbao': 31, 'Fluminense': 20, 'Santos': 20, 'Internacional': 20, 'Botafogo': 20, 'Clube Sport Marítimo': 23, 'Real Sporting de Gijón': 30, 'Bahia': 20, 'Atlético Paranaense': 20, 'Santos Laguna': 26, 'Sport Club do Recife': 20, 'Sporting Kansas City': 27, 'Chapecoense': 20, 'Ceará Sporting Club': 20, 'Sporting de Charleroi': 28, 'Sporting Lokeren': 28, 'Wigan Athletic': 30, 'Charlton Athletic': 28, 'Oldham Athletic': 25, 'VfL Sportfreunde Lotte': 28, \"St. Patrick's Athletic\": 23}\n","metadata":{"output":"FIFA BR clubs: {'Sporting CP': 30, 'Atlético Mineiro': 20, 'Cruzeiro': 20, 'Athletic Club de Bilbao': 31, 'Fluminense': 20, 'Santos': 20, 'Internacional': 20, 'Botafogo': 20, 'Clube Sport Marítimo': 23, 'Real Sporting de Gijón': 30, 'Bahia': 20, 'Atlético Paranaense': 20, 'Santos Laguna': 26, 'Sport Club do Recife': 20, 'Sporting Kansas City': 27, 'Chapecoense': 20, 'Ceará Sporting Club': 20, 'Sporting de Charleroi': 28, 'Sporting Lokeren': 28, 'Wigan Athletic': 30, 'Charlton Athletic': 28, 'Oldham Athletic': 25, 'VfL Sportfreunde Lotte': 28, \"St. Patrick's Athletic\": 23}\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"./venv/bin/python << 'EOF'\nimport csv, collections, unicodedata, re\n\ndef unaccent(s):\n    return ''.join(c for c in unicodedata.normalize('NFKD', s) if not unicodedata.combining(c))\n\n# FIFA Brazilian clubs (clubs that look Brazilian)\nwith open('data/kaggle/fifa_data.csv', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    clubs = collections.Counter(row['Club'] for row in csv.DictReader(f))\nbrazilian = ['Flamengo','Palmeiras','São Paulo','Santos','Grêmio','Corinthians','Athletico','Atlético','Mineiro','Paranaense','Bahia','Vasco','Botafogo','Cruzeiro','Fluminense','Internacional','Goiás','Sport','Chapecoense','Ceará','Fortaleza','América','Avaí','Criciúma','Paysandu','Goiás','Coritiba','Vitória','Bahia','Athletic']\nhits = {c: n for c, n in clubs.items() if any(b.lower() in unaccent(c).lower() for b in brazilian)}\nprint('FIFA BR clubs:', hits)\nEOF","time":{"start":1788236797997,"end":1788236798000}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"This confirms the design: club identity must consider base+state, with fallbacks. Big famous clubs appear without state (\"flamengo\", \"cruzeiro\") and with state (\"Flamengo-RJ\"). The resolution:\n\nCanonical ID = `base` when unambiguous, else `base-state`. For ambiguous bases (atletico, america, botafogo, internacional, santos, etc.), the state suffix is REQUIRED for identity; a bare \"atletico\" without state... when would that occur? In Libertadores: \"Atlético-MG\", \"Atlético Nacional\" (COL — \"Atletico Nacional\" base without state, different club!), \"Atletico Tucuman\" (ARG). So bare bases like \"atletico nacional\", \"atletico tucuman\" are distinct full names. Bare \"atletico\" alone probably never appears. But \"Athletico\" (Libertadores 2020 NA row: \"Athletico\") appears bare! And \"palmeiras\", \"flamengo\" bare in Libertadores.\n\nSo resolution strategy:\n1. For each name, extract (base, state).\n2. If base in ambiguous set: need state → id = f\"{base}-{state}\"; if no state, try to infer: \"Athletico\" (bare) → athletico-pr (Athletico Paranaense, the only club spelled \"Athletico\" with H!). \"Atletico\" bare → ambiguous, resolve via unique alias mapping or leave fuzzy. In practice: alias map handles \"athletico\" → \"atletico-pr\". Actually spelling \"athletico\" (with h) uniquely identifies Paranaense. And \"atletico\" bare → probably never in data; if user asks \"Atletico\", fuzzy match should return multiple options — resolve_team returns candidates.\n3. If base unambiguous: id = base (state ignored for identity, e.g. \"Flamengo-RJ\" and \"Flamengo-PI\"?? — wait, \"flamengo\" has PI and RJ collisions! Flamengo-PI is a tiny club from Piauí in Copa do Brasil early rounds. Hmm! So even \"flamengo\" is ambiguous: Flamengo-RJ (the famous one) vs Flamengo-PI. Same for santos: \"Santos-AP\" (Santos-AP is a small Amapá club) vs Santos-SP (the famous one).\n\nUgh. So identity = base+state whenever state present. For bare names (Libertadores \"Flamengo\", BRFB \"Flamengo\", hist? hist has suffixes mostly, FIFA \"Flamengo\") — those are the FAMOUS clubs (Libertadores group stage participants from Brazil are the big ones; but \"Santos-AP\" never in Libertadores... Actually wait, Libertadores has \"Barcelona-EQU\", \"Nacional (URU)\" — foreign clubs. Bare \"Santos\" in Libertadores = Santos-SP. Bare \"Flamengo\" = Flamengo-RJ.)\n\nSo rule: id = f\"{base}-{state}\" if state present, else... for bare names I need to map to the famous club. Approach: \n- When state present: id = base-state (e.g. \"flamengo-pi\", \"flamengo-rj\", \"santos-sp\").\n- When state absent: if base is ambiguous (has multiple states across dataset): map to the MAJOR club via curated map: flamengo→flamengo-rj, santos→santos-sp, botafogo→botafogo-rj, internacional→internacional-rs, atletico→??? bare \"atletico\" rare; \"athletico\"→atletico-pr (unique spelling), america→america-mg (or ambiguous — America-RN played Série A 2007ish; bare \"America\" in hist 2003-2019: America-RN was in Série A 2007. Hmm, hist rows: 'América-MG' and 'América-RN' both have suffixes. Bare \"America\" probably only in BRFB? BRFB has \"America MG\"? and maybe \"America RN\". Copa do Brasil: 'América - MG', 'América - RN' — suffixed. So bare \"america\" rare; FIFA club \"América (MG)\"? FIFA 19 has \"América Mineiro\"? Let me check FIFA Brazilian clubs.)\n- If base unambiguous: id = base.\n\nCurated major-club map for ambiguous bases:\n- flamengo → flamengo-rj\n- santos → santos-sp\n- botafogo → botafogo-rj\n- internacional → internacional-rs\n- america → america-mg\n- atletico → atletico-mg? Hmm. \"Atletico-MG\" is more famous, but bare \"Atletico\" — the Libertadores NA row \"Athletico\" (with h). Bare \"atletico\" (no h) doesn't occur. I'll map \"athletico\" → atletico-pr, and bare \"atletico\" → ambiguous (return candidates) or default atletico-mg. Let me check the actual data for bare occurrences.\n- vitoria → vitoria-ba (Vitória-BA vs Vitória-ES: Rio Branco-ES collision? 'vitoria' appears with which states? Only BA listed? The collision list shows 'vitoria' NOT in collisions... it wasn't listed! Wait, collisions list: botafogo, internacional, atletico, flamengo, nautico, santos, santa cruz, america, juventude, guarani, comercial, rio branco, sao raimundo, bragantino, operario, ypiranga. \"vitoria\" not there — good, only Vitória-BA exists.\n- guarani → guarani-sp (Guarani-CE is small; famous Guarani is SP — but careful: hist 2003-2019 Guarani (SP) played Série B/C. BRFB? Copa do Brasil Guarani-CE. Bare \"Guarani\" in hist = Guarani-SP. Map bare guarani → guarani-sp.)\n- bragantino → bragantino-sp (RB Bragantino; Bragantino-PA is small)\n- operario → operario-ms (Operário-MS vs Operário-PR; famous is Operário-MS in Série B recently. Bare \"Operario\" in BRFB? BRFB has \"Operario MS\"? need check. Default operario-ms.)\n- santa cruz → santa cruz-pe\n- nautico → nautico-pe\n- juventude → juventude-rs\n- rio branco, sao raimundo, comercial, ypiranga → rare; default to any.\n\nHmm, this is getting complex but it's THE core challenge of this dataset (\"Implementation should normalize team names for consistent matching\"). I'll implement:\n\n1. `normalize(name)` → (base, state): strip parens, strip accents, lowercase, extract state suffix.\n2. Alias table: full-name aliases → (base, state): e.g. \"atletico mineiro\"→(\"atletico\",\"mg\"), \"atletico goianiense\"→(\"atletico\",\"go\"), \"atletico paranaense\"/\"athletico paranaense\"→(\"atletico\",\"pr\"), \"america mineiro\"→(\"america\",\"mg\"), \"botafogo rj\"... wait BRFB \"Botafogo RJ\" already has state suffix pattern \"RJ\"? My state regex looks for \"-XX\" at end. \"Botafogo RJ\" has space not dash. Need regex to catch \" Botafogo RJ\" → base \"botafogo\", state \"RJ\": pattern `\\s[-–]\\s*([A-Z]{2})$` or `\\s+([A-Z]{2})$`. Careful: \"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\" ends with \"Paulista\" not state. OK, extend regex: `(?:\\s*[-–]\\s*|\\s+)([A-Z]{2})$`.\n   - \"ec bahia\" → bahia; \"vasco da gama rj\" → (\"vasco\",\"rj\")→ base \"vasco da gama\"? I want \"vasco da gama\" and \"vasco\" same → canonical base \"vasco\" via alias \"vasco da gama\"→\"vasco\".\n   - \"athletic club mg\" → ? Athletic Club (MG) is a small club in Série C. base \"athletic\", state mg. OK generic.\n   - \"atletico mineiro\" alias is important.\n3. Canonical id: `base-state` if state else base; then apply ambiguous-base defaults: if no state and base in ambiguous set → default state from curated map.\n4. Then id normalization pass #2: some ids differ only by alias (\"atletico-pr\" from \"Athletico-PR\" and alias \"athletico paranaense\" → (\"atletico\",\"pr\") → id \"atletico-pr\"). Consistent.\n\n5. Display names: curated map for major clubs: {\"flamengo-rj\": \"Flamengo\", \"atletico-mg\": \"Atlético Mineiro\", ...}; fallback: title-case base + state.\n\n6. User resolution: `resolve(query)`: normalize query → id; if id in registry → done; else substring/fuzzy search over registry ids and display names → return best match + alternatives. E.g. \"Corinthians\" → \"corinthians\"; \"Palmeiras-SP\" → \"palmeiras\"; \"Atletico Mineiro\" → \"atletico-mg\"; \"SPFC\"?? too far, skip.\n\nForeign clubs in Libertadores: \"Boca Juniors\", \"River Plate\", \"Nacional (URU)\" → base \"nacional\" (paren stripped). Fine — they're just teams in the dataset for h2h purposes (\"Show me all Copa Libertadores finals\" includes them).\n\nFIFA clubs: \"Paris Saint-Germain\", \"Liverpool\"... For team_players(\"Flamengo\") need to match FIFA Club \"Flamengo\" → fifa club name matching: normalize FIFA club names similarly (accents: \"São Paulo\" → sao paulo; \"Grêmio\" → gremio; \"Palmeiras\"; \"Athletico Paranaense\"? FIFA 19 has \"Athletico-PR\"? no — FIFA 19 Brazilian clubs: Grêmio, Palmeiras, Flamengo, São Paulo, Santos, Sport? Let me check.)\n\nLet me now check FIFA Brazilian clubs and bare-name occurrences in data. Then write the implementation.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b38176f001VBSxLLTmZBmmp3","sessionID":"ses_fa4ccfc0bffexSFu2vIRQjobrF","messageID":"msg_05b370d4d001Ua2dANPdp7IDMo"}}
