n order:\n1. Get (rawbase, suffix) after cleanup.\n2. Apply alias map to rawbase → possibly (base, state) or canonical id.\n3. If suffix present: id_candidate = base + \"-\" + suffix.lower().\n4. If no suffix: if base ambiguous → default state → id. Else id = base.\n5. Unification: maintain registry of all ids seen; two ids refer to same club only via alias map. \"corinthians-sp\" vs \"corinthians\": PROBLEM.\n\nFix: make the state suffix NOT part of identity when the (base, state) pair's base is unambiguous IGNORING the suffix, i.e.: if base+other-states has exactly one \"real\" club... but flamengo has 2 real clubs. Ugh.\n\nSimpler robust fix: compute identity as follows:\n- id_stateful = base-suffix (or base if none).\n- Ambiguity set = bases having ≥2 distinct suffixes among BRAZILIAN states, or appearing bare+suffix.\n- If base unambiguous (only one Brazilian state suffix ever seen, or only bare): strip suffix → id = base. (corinthians-sp → corinthians; santos-equi? no that's barcelona-equi... santos-sp/santos-ap → ambiguous)\n- If base ambiguous: keep suffix; bare → DEFAULT_STATE map (famous club). If no default (e.g. truly unknown), fall back to base id and mark ambiguity.\n\nForeign 3-letter suffixes: \"barcelona-equ\" — base \"barcelona\" only ever with -equ in matches, bare in FIFA. If I treat foreign suffix like state for identity: \"barcelona\" ambiguous (equ + bare FIFA) → bare needs default... but they're DIFFERENT clubs! FC Barcelona ≠ Barcelona SC (Ecuador). So: foreign-suffixed ids NEVER unify with bare. I.e., foreign suffix = always part of id (never stripped); Brazilian state suffix = part of id only if base is ambiguous among Brazilian clubs. That's the rule!\n\nSo:\n- \"Barcelona-EQU\" → id \"barcelona-equ\" (foreign, keep).\n- \"FC Barcelona\" (FIFA) → id \"barcelona\".\n- \"Corinthians-SP\" → base corinthians, Brazilian suffix, unambiguous base → id \"corinthians\".\n- \"Flamengo-RJ\"/\"Flamengo\" → id \"flamengo-rj\" (ambiguous: pi+rj+bare). Bare→default RJ.\n- \"Palmeiras-SP\"/\"Palmeiras\" → unambiguous → \"palmeiras\".\n- \"Atletico-MG\" → ambiguous base (mg/pr/go/ba/es/ac...) → \"atletico-mg\" ✓. Alias \"Atletico Mineiro\" → explicitly mapped to \"atletico-mg\" ✓. \"Atlético Paranaense\" → \"atletico-pr\" ✓.\n- \"Sport-PE\" → base \"sport\": any other club named Sport? \"Sport Club do Recife\" alias → sport-pe. \"Sport Recife\" → sport-pe. Is bare \"sport\" ambiguous? Only PE. So unambiguous → id \"sport\". Hmm — but alias maps full names to \"sport-pe\"... I'd have alias point to canonical id AFTER unification: alias \"sport club do recife\" → base \"sport\" (strip fillers via alias) → unambiguous → id \"sport\". OK I'll implement aliases as base-normalizers (full name → base), then the state logic applies uniformly:\n  - \"atletico mineiro\" → base \"atletico\", state \"mg\" (alias carries state)\n  - \"sport club do recife\" → base \"sport\" (no state) → id \"sport\"\n  - \"ceara sporting club\" → base \"ceara\" → id \"ceara\"\n  - \"vasco da gama\" → base \"vasco\" → ambiguous? vasco bare + \"vasco da gama rj\" → base \"vasco\"... \"Vasco-AC\"?? there is \"Rio Branco-AC\"... vasco: states? From collision scan, 'vasco' wasn't in collisions (only bare count). Wait the bare counter showed vasco: 3 in Libertadores, 276 in hist — and BRFB \"vasco da gama rj\" has state. If vasco never has another state → unambiguous → id \"vasco\". Then alias \"vasco da gama\"→\"vasco\" ✓. \n\nDEFAULT_STATE needed for: flamengo(rj), santos(sp), botafogo(rj), internacional(rs), america(mg), atletico(mg), athletico(pr→base atletico), guarani(sp), bragantino(sp), operario(ms), santa cruz(pe), nautico(pe), juventude(rs), comercial(?), rio branco(?), sao raimundo(?), ypiranga(?).\n\nHmm wait, one more check: \"america\" — America-RN played in hist Série A (2007). Bare \"America\" anywhere? From bare-scan: no bare \"america\" in match files (only in FIFA? FIFA doesn't have America... \"América (MX)\"! Mexican club \"Améric