' in n.lower() or 'connected' in n.lower()])\nimport inspect\nprint(inspect.signature(mem.create_connected_server_and_client_session))\nEOF","time":{"start":1788237068180,"end":1788237068215}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"FIFA 19 has 13 Brazilian clubs × 20 players. Flamengo/Palmeiras/Corinthians/São Paulo/Vasco aren't there (PES exclusives in 2019). Grêmio IS there (I missed it in the earlier probe because the name is 'Grêmio' — my filter had 'Grêmio' accented... unaccent both sides... whatever, it's confirmed now).\n\nTop Brazilian players in this FIFA data: Neymar 92, then Casemiro/Coutinho/Marcelo/Thiago Silva 88. (Alisson 89? Not in list — Alisson is in FIFA 19... maybe nationality is \"Brazil\"... let me not worry; tests will assert Neymar is #1 and count 827.)\n\nNow let me finalize and write the code. Plan:\n\n**Files:**\n1. `brazilian_soccer_mcp/__init__.py`\n2. `brazilian_soccer_mcp/models.py` — Match, Player dataclasses\n3. `brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalizer.py` — team name normalization + registry + derbies\n4. `brazilian_soccer_mcp/loaders.py` — CSV loaders, date parsing\n5. `brazilian_soccer_mcp/service.py` — query service (all business logic, returns structured + formatted)\n6. `brazilian_soccer_mcp/server.py` — FastMCP tool definitions\n7. `server.py` — root entrypoint\n8. `requirements.txt`\n9. `pytest.ini` or pyproject section\n10. `tests/conftest.py` + BDD test files (GWT structured)\n11. Update `README.md`\n\nLet me write each file carefully with detailed context block comments at the start (the prompts.txt hint mentions \"Maintain a detailed context block comment at the start of every code file\" as a sample variation — TASK.md itself doesn't require it, but it's good practice and matches the house style described; I'll include concise module docstrings explaining context, why, what).\n\n**Key implementation details:**\n\nnormalizer.py:\n- `BRAZILIAN_STATES`: 27 abbrevs (AC, AL, AP, AM, BA, CE, DF, ES, GO, MA, MT, MS, MG, PA, PB, PR, PE, PI, RJ, RN, RS, RO, RR, SC, SP, SE, TO).\n- `ALIASES`: dict normalized-full-name → (base, state|None):\n  - \"atletico mineiro\" → (\"atletico\",\"mg\")\n  - \"atletico paranaense\"/\"athletico paranaense\" → (\"atletico\",\"pr\")\n  - \"atletico goianiense\" → (\"atletico\",\"go\")\n  - \"america mineiro\"/\"america de caldas\"? no. \"america mineiro\" → (\"america\",\"mg\")\n  - \"america rj\"? America-RJ (old)... not needed.\n  - \"vasco da gama\" → (\"vasco\", None)\n  - \"sport club do recife\"/\"sport recife\"/\"sport club recife\" → (\"sport\", None)\n  - \"ceara sporting club\" → (\"ceara\", None)\n  - \"athletic club\" → (\"athletic\", None)  # Athletic Club MG (Série C)\n  - \"botafogo de futebol e regatas\" → (\"botafogo\",\"rj\")\n  - \"botafogo sp\"? BRFB has \"Botafogo SP\" with suffix already.\n  - \"ec bahia\"/\"esporte clube bahia e vitoria\"?? BRFB \"EC Bahia\" → (\"bahia\", None)\n  - \"gremio foot ball porto alegrense\" → (\"gremio\", None)\n  - \"sao paulo fc\" → (\"sao paulo\", None)\n  - \"corinthians sp\"? BRFB: \"Corinthians\"? not present. add \"sport club corinthins paulista\"? The spec mentions \"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\" → (\"corinthians\", None)\n  - \"clube atletico mineiro\" → (\"atletico\",\"mg\")\n  - \"gremio fbpa\"? skip.\n  - \"red bull bragantino\" → (\"bragantino\",\"sp\")\n  - \"rb bragantino\" → (\"bragantino\",\"sp\")\n  - \"operario ferroviario\" → (\"operario\",\"ms\")\n  - \"guarani fc\"? → (\"guarani\", \"sp\")? careful — Guarani FC (SP, Campinas) famous. \"guarani fc\" → (\"guarani\",\"sp\") ok.\n  - \"fluminense fc\" → (\"fluminense\", None)\n  - \"clube de regatas do flamengo\" → (\"flamengo\",\"rj\")\n- `DEFAULT_STATES` (famous club defaults for ambiguous bare bases):\n  flamengo→rj, santos→sp, botafogo→rj, internacional→rs, america→mg, atletico→mg, guarani→sp, bragantino→sp, operario→ms, santa cruz→pe, nautico→pe, juventude→rs, comercial→ms? (Comercial-MS vs Comercial-PI — famous Comercial (Ribeirão Preto, SP)?? Hmm — Comercial-SP (Ribeirão Preto) is the famous one! But collision list shows comercial MS & PI. Hist bare \"Comercial\"? The bare scan showed no bare comercial. Default doesn't matter much; use \"sp\"? Comercial-SP isn't even in the collision list. I'll set comercial→ms (Comercial-MS played Série B/C more recently? Actually Comercial-MS (Campo Grande)... whatever, bare never occurs). rio branco→ac? (Rio Branco-AC famous-ish), sao raimundo→rr? no (São Raimundo-RR? famous São Raimundo is PA? collisions PA/RR... skip: leave unmapped → resolve returns candidates).\n  For unmapped ambiguous bare bases: pick the state with the most matches (frequency-based default) — elegant fallback! DEFAULT_STATES is just an override for cases where frequency would mislead (flamengo-rj obviously most frequent anyway; frequency default works for all famous clubs!). Actually frequency-based default handles everything: bare \"flamengo\" → most common flamengo-XX = flamengo-rj ✓; bare \"atletico\" → atletico-mg (most common) ✓ (bare \"atletico\" doesn't occur anyway); bare \"athletico\" → alias to atletico-pr (spelling-specific: \"athletico\" base → treat as alias of (\"atletico\",\"pr\")!). \n\n  Special: \"athletico\" (bare, from Libertadores NA row and maybe others) → the club Athletico-PR. I'll add alias \"athletico\" → (\"atletico\",\"pr\"). But wait: BRFB \"Athletic Club MG\" → base \"athletic club\" → alias → (\"athletic\", None) → id \"athletic\". Hmm \"athletic\" vs \"athletico\" distinct bases ✓.\n\n- Parsing steps for `parse_name(raw)`:\n  1. `raw.strip()`; strip quotes.\n  2. Replace trailing parenthetical country `(...)` of 2-4 uppercase letters → foreign_suffix (e.g. URU, PAR, EQU). Multiple? Just one.\n  3. Remove other parenthetical content (notes like \"(antigo Esporte Clube Barreira)\").\n  4. Extract trailing Brazilian state: regex `(?:\\s*[-–]\\s*|\\s+)([A-Z]{2})$` where group in BRAZILIAN_STATES. Note: must be uppercase 2 letters in ORIGINAL string (before lowercasing).\n  5. Unaccent + lowercase base; collapse whitespace.\n  6. Alias lookup on base (with suffix-less base): if in ALIASES → override (base, state).\n  7. Return ParsedName(base, state, foreign_suffix).\n  \n  Careful: step 4 regex on names like \"América - MG\" → base \"América\", state MG ✓. \"Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira) - RJ\": parens stripped first → \"Boavista Sport Club  - RJ\" → state RJ, base \"boavista sport club\". Hmm — \"boavista sport club\" as base is fine (id \"boavista sport club\" — ugly but consistent; only appears in Copa do Brasil; display = original). Maybe strip filler words from base: tokens {fc,ec,sc,ac,ca,clube,club,esporte,esportes,futebol,de,do,da}? \"boavista sport club\" → \"boavista sport\"?? But \"sport\" must be kept (\"Sport-PE\" → \"sport\"!). Danger: filler stripping changes \"sport club do recife\" but that's in ALIASES already. I'll only strip TRAILING filler words when what remains is non-empty AND not exactly \"sport\": e.g. \"boavista sport club\" → strip \"club\" → \"boavista sport\"; \"ec bahia\" → \"bahia\"; \"athletic club\" → handled by alias. But \"sport club do recife\" → strip \"do recife\"?? No — only strip TRAILING fillers one by one: \"sport club do recife\": trailing \"recife\" not filler → stop → \"sport club do recife\" (alias anyway). \"ceara sporting club\" → alias. \"botafogo rj\"? state extraction handles. Hmm \"Athletic Club MG\": state regex `\\s+([A-Z]{2})$` matches \"MG\" ✓ → base \"athletic club\" → trailing filler \"club\" → \"athletic\" ✓ id \"athletic\". And \"boavista sport club\" → \"boavista sport\"? then display \"Boavista Sport Club\"... id \"boavista sport\". Only appears in cup data with full name consistently? It appears as home/away with same string — consistent either way. OK but wait: trailing-filler strip must NOT strip \"sport\" — filler set = {fc, ec, sc, ac, ca, clube, club, sporting?, ...} — do NOT include \"sport\", \"esporte\"? \"Esporte\" appears in \"Fortaleza Esporte Clube\" → strip \"clube\" → \"fortaleza esporte\" → strip \"esporte\"? If \"esporte\" in fillers → \"fortaleza\" ✓. But \"Sport\" (Recife) never trailing after stripping... \"Sport-PE\" → base \"sport\" — is \"sport\" a filler? NO, must not strip. Filler set: {\"fc\",\"ec\",\"sc\",\"ac\",\"ca\",\"clube\",\"club\",\"esporte\",\"esportes\",\"futebol\",\"futebool\",\"sporting\"}? \"sporting\" — \"Ceará Sporting Club\" is aliased; \"Sporting CP\" (FIFA) — FIFA clubs matched separately. Hmm, but trailing-strip with \"sporting\" would turn \"ceara sporting club\"→\"ceara sporting\"→? \"sporting\" not trailing yet... order: strip trailing tokens repeatedly while trailing token ∈ fillers: \"ceara sporting club\" → strip \"club\" → strip \"sporting\" → \"ceara\" ✓ (alias redundant then!). \"sport club do recife\" → trailing \"recife\" not filler → stop ✓ (alias needed). Nice — with fillers {fc,ec,sc,ac,ca,clube,club,esporte,esportes,futebol,sporting}, aliases needed only for multi-word official names: atletico mineiro, atletico paranaense, vasco da gama, sport club do recife, red bull bragantino, botafogo de futebol e regatas, etc. Plus \"sao paulo fc\" → strip \"fc\" → \"sao paulo\" ✓ no alias needed! \n\n  FILLERS = {\"fc\",\"ec\",\"sc\",\"ac\",\"ca\",\"clube\",\"club\",\"esporte\",\"esportes\",\"futebol\",\"futebool\",\"sporting\",\"sub\"?} — hmm \"sc\" would strip from \"SC Internacional\"→\"internacional\" ✓. But careful: \"AC\" — \"AC Goianiense\"? fine.\n  Edge: base becomes empty (name was just \"FC\"?) — guard: if empty, keep original base.\n\n- Registry: built after loading: `ambiguous_bases` = bases (Brazilian, i.e. having a Brazilian state variant OR bare) with >1 distinct Brazilian state suffixes, OR (bare + ≥1 state suffix AND that base... hmm). Wait — unambiguous definition: base has exactly ONE Brazilian state suffix across registry AND (bare occurrences refer to that same club — always true if only one state club exists with that base). So:\n  - states_of_base = {state for all names with this base and Brazilian state}\n  - if len(states_of_base) == 0 → id = base (pure bare names, e.g. \"boca juniors\", \"river plate\", \"palmeiras\"? no palmeiras has -SP suffix... \"palmeiras\": states {sp} → id \"palmeiras\" ✓)\n  - if len == 1 → id = base (suffix stripped)\n  - if len ≥ 2 → suffix required: id = base-state; bare → frequency default (most matches) or DEFAULT_STATES override.\n  \n  Foreign-suffixed (URU/PAR/EQU): id = base + \"-\" + suffix.lower() ALWAYS (never stripped, never merged with bare). E.g. \"nacional-uru\", \"nacional-par\", \"olimpia-par\", \"barcelona-equ\", \"nacional\" bare (if exists, e.g. Ecuador club Nacional? Libertadores has \"Nacional (URU)\" and \"Nacional (PAR)\" — both suffixed. OK.)\n\n- `display_name(id)`: curated DISPLAY map for famous ids (Flamengo, Palmeiras, Atlético Mineiro, Athletico Paranaense, São Paulo, Grêmio, etc. — ~40 clubs with proper accents), else derive from best original variant (title case, keep accents of the first-seen original). I'll keep a map id → most frequent original raw name, title-cased.\n\n- `resolve_team(query)`: parse query → id; if in registry → TeamRef(id, display, exact=True). Else substring search over ids + display names + original variants; if exactly 1 → it; if several → return candidates list. Also special: if query parses to bare ambiguous base with no registry hit → frequency default. Fuzzy: difflib.get_close_matches over ids.\n\n- DERBY registry (normalized id pairs):\n  - Fla-Flu: flamengo-rj / fluminense\n  - Clássico dos Milhões: flamengo-rj / vasco\n  - Majestoso: corinthians / sao paulo\n  - Choque-Rei: palmeiras / sao paulo\n  - Derby Paulista: palmeiras / corinthians\n  - Grenal: gremio / internacional-rs\n  - Clássico Vovô: fluminense? No — Vovô is Fluminense? Clássico Vovô = Fluminense? No! Clássico Vovô is Flamengo?? Let me recall: Clássico Vovô = Fluminense vs Botafogo? No — \"Vovô