"NA\"/\"\" → None.\n- `load_matches(data_dir)` → (matches, registry): reads 5 match CSVs, skips fully-broken rows (no date AND no goals; or missing team), tags competition:\n  - Brasileirao_Matches.csv → competition \"Brasileirão Série A\", source \"Brasileirao_Matches.csv\"\n  - novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv → competition \"Brasileirão Série A\" too?? Hmm — dedup problem for standings. I'll tag both as \"Brasileirão Série A\" but with source distinguishing; service's `canonical Brasileirão` view picks preferred source per season: 2003-2011 novo, 2012-2022 Brasileirao_Matches, 2023 BRFB Serie A. And general match search dedups by (date, home_id, away_id) preferring the primary source.\n  \n  Hmm wait — simpler idea: mark DUPLICATES at load: after loading everything, group by (date, home_id, away_id, home_goals, away_goals); for identical matches keep the one from preferred source (source_priority: Brasileirao_Matches > Libertadores_Matches > Brazilian_Cup_Matches > novo > BRFB?) — but cross-competition dup: Brasileirao_Matches and novo both \"Série A 2012-2019\" → same competition → same (date,home,away) → dedup within competition keeps primary. BRFB Copa do Brasil vs Brazilian_Cup_Matches: same competition \"Copa do Brasil\", overlapping years 2014-2022! E.g. 2019 cup matches in both files → dedup by (competition, date, home, away). But BRFB covers 2014-2023 while Brazilian_Cup covers 2012-2021 — Brazilian_Cup 2021 vs BRFB 2021 both exist. Dedup key must include score? If scores conflict... shouldn't. Keep key (competition, season, date, home_id, away_id); prefer source Brazilian_Cup_Matches over BRFB for Copa do Brasil; for Série A prefer Brasileirao_Matches > novo > BRFB.\n  \n  Wait, but are BRFB Copa do Brasil matches the same matches as Brazilian_Cup_Matches? BRFB Copa do Brasil 2015: 139 matches; Brazilian_Cup 2015: 158. Different coverage (BRFB maybe only some rounds). Overlapping matches dedup fine.\n  \n  Série B/C only in BRFB — no dedup issue.\n  Libert