lso support `--transport streamable-http`? Keep stdio default; optional SSE? stdio only, simple.\n\nTests (BDD GWT): pytest classes with Gherkin docstrings and Given/When/Then comments:\n- tests/conftest.py — `service` fixture (session-scoped, real data), `mcp_client` fixture using FastMCP in-memory session. In mcp 2.1.1: `from mcp.shared.memory import create_connected_server_and_client_session` — verify import path. Also `mcp.client.session.Client` etc. Let me check the mcp package API in venv.\n- test_normalizer.py — name variation scenarios (accented/suffixed/aliases/collisions).\n- test_loaders.py — all 6 files load, counts match spec (4180, 1337, 1255-1NA?, 10296, 6886, 18207), date parsing formats, UTF-8 names.\n- test_match_queries.py — GWT: Flamengo vs Fluminense matches exist w/ date+score+competition; Palmeiras 2023 matches (BRFB!); Copa Libertadores finals; date-range queries; cross-file dedup.\n- test_team_queries.py — Corinthians home record 2022 (compute from data — verify first); Palmeiras 2023 stats; h2h.\n- test_player_queries.py — Brazilian players count 827; Neymar top; Santos squad 20; positions filter.\n- test_competition_queries.py — 2019 Brasileirão champion Flamengo 90 pts; standings have 20 teams; relegated 2020 (4 bottom); Libertadores 2019 winner Flamengo; seasons lists.\n- test_statistics.py — biggest wins; avg goals ~2.4-2.5 (verify); home win rate ~50%; best home/away records; compare seasons.\n- test_server.py — MCP tools callable in-memory: list_tools ≥ 15; call search_matches & search_players & standings end-to-end.\n\nTest data verification: I must verify expected values BEFORE baking into assertions (Corinthians home 2022, avg goals, relegation 2020, Libertadores finals count, etc.). I'll write the service first, then explore via the service, then finalize test expectations.\n\nmcp in-memory client check needed. Let me check the mcp package API quickly.\n\nPerformance: load time — 42k rows CSV with csv module ~1-2s. FIFA 18k rows f