nly registers MATCH data names, not FIFA clubs (FIFA clubs matched separately). But \"Botafogo RJ\" (BRFB) → space regex ✓ (Botafogo, rj). \"America MG\" ✓. Careful about false positives in match data: \"Moto Club MA\" → (\"moto club\",\"ma\") → base after filler strip: \"moto\"?? trailing \"club\" is filler → \"moto club\"→\"moto\"! Then id \"moto-ma\". Hmm wait: filler strip removes \"club\" → base \"moto\". Provisional \"moto-ma\". Any other \"moto\"? No. Unambiguous → canonical... wait ambiguous check: base \"moto\" states {ma} → unambiguous → remap \"moto-ma\" → \"moto\". Display fallback: \"Moto Club MA\".title() = \"Moto Club Ma\" — ugly. Whatever, it's a Serie C/D club. Actually wait — will \"moto\" collide with anything? No. OK.\n\nFalse positive risk for _STATE_SPACE_RE: names ending in two capital letters that aren't states, e.g. \"CSA\" (3 letters, no); \"CRB\" no; \"ABC\" no. \"...EC\"?? e.g. \"Fortaleza EC\" → trailing \"EC\" — is EC in BRAZILIAN_STATES? NO (not a state abbrev) ✓ safe. \"...SC\"? \"SC\" not a state ✓. \"...SP\"? only if actually state. OK good — because state check filters.\n\nBUT WAIT: \"Figueirense FC\"? → \"fc\" not state ✓. \"Bahia de Feira - BA\" ✓.\n\nOne more: BRFB \"Atletico Goianiense\" → alias ✓ → (\"atletico\",\"go\") → atletico-go ✓.\n\nBRFB \"Athletic Club MG\" → space-state MG ✓ base \"athletic club\" → filler strip → \"athletic\" → provisional \"athletic-mg\". Base \"athletic\" states {mg} → unambiguous → canonical \"athletic\". ✓ distinct from atletico-* ✓.\n\nHmm — but is \"athletic-mg\" vs canonical \"athletic\": display \"Athletic Club MG\"? fallback most-common raw = \"Athletic Club MG\" — good display actually.\n\nHist file: \"Athletico-PR\" → base \"athletico\" → ALIAS (\"atletico\",\"pr\") ✓. But CAREFUL: alias applied AFTER state extraction: parse \"Athletico-PR\": state PR extracted, base \"athletico\", alias → (\"atletico\", pr) but state already \"pr\" → stays ✓ → atletico-pr ✓.\n\nAlias state conflict: \"Atl