{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788237733891,"sessionID":"ses_fa4ccfc0bffexSFu2vIRQjobrF","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_8d756680da4b43b7af126f25","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"./venv/bin/python << 'EOF'\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.loaders import load_all\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.models import BRASILEIRAO_A\ndata = load_all('data/kaggle')\n# how many 2019 Serie A matches per source?\nfrom collections import Counter\nc = Counter(m.source for m in data.matches if m.competition==BRASILEIRAO_A and m.season==2019)\nprint(c)\n# check: same fixture (home,away,score) from different sources with different dates?\nseen = {}\nmismatch = 0\nfor m in data.matches:\n    if m.competition==BRASILEIRAO_A and m.season==2019:\n        key = (m.home_id, m.away_id, m.home_goals, m.away_goals)\n        if key in seen and seen[key][0].date != m.date:\n            mismatch += 1\n        seen.setdefault(key, []).append(m)\nprint(\"fixtures total:\", len(data.matches and [m for m in data.matches if m.competition==BRASILEIRAO_A and m.season==2019]))\nprint(\"unique fixtures (home,away,score):\", len(seen))\nprint(\"date mismatches between sources:\", mismatch)\nEOF"},"output":"Counter({'Brasileirao_Matches.csv': 380, 'BR-Football-Dataset.csv': 112, 'novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv': 2})\nfixtures total: 494\nunique fixtures (home,away,score): 418\ndate mismatches between sources: 76\n","metadata":{"output":"Counter({'Brasileirao_Matches.csv': 380, 'BR-Football-Dataset.csv': 112, 'novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv': 2})\nfixtures total: 494\nunique fixtures (home,away,score): 418\ndate mismatches between sources: 76\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"./venv/bin/python << 'EOF'\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.loaders import load_all\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.models import BRASILEIRAO_A\ndata = load_all('data/kaggle')\n# how many 2019 Serie A matches per source?\nfrom collections import Counter\nc = Counter(m.source for m in data.matches if m.competition==BRASILEIRAO_A and m.season==2019)\nprint(c)\n# check: same fixture (home,away,score) from different sources with different dates?\nseen = {}\nmismatch = 0\nfor m in data.matches:\n    if m.competition==BRASILEIRAO_A and m.season==2019:\n        key = (m.home_id, m.away_id, m.home_goals, m.away_goals)\n        if key in seen and seen[key][0].date != m.date:\n            mismatch += 1\n        seen.setdefault(key, []).append(m)\nprint(\"fixtures total:\", len(data.matches and [m for m in data.matches if m.competition==BRASILEIRAO_A and m.season==2019]))\nprint(\"unique fixtures (home,away,score):\", len(seen))\nprint(\"date mismatches between sources:\", mismatch)\nEOF","time":{"start":1788237733865,"end":1788237733889}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Normalization works, but the 2019 Série A standings show 22 teams and ~49-52 matches per team — the double-counting problem I anticipated: Brasileirão_Matches 2019 (380 matches) + novo 2019 (380 matches) + BRFB Serie A 2019 (~380) were NOT fully deduplicated. Only 5134 dupes removed total. Why? The dedup key is (competition, season, date, home_id, away_id). If novo records a different date for the same fixture (or Brasileirao_Matches and novo have different home/away assignments?), the dupes survive.\n\nExpected matches for 2019 Série A: 380. Got 49*... ~1050 total (22 teams). So ~2.7x duplication. Let me diagnose: compare per-source match sets for 2019.\n\nPossible causes:\n1. novo 2019 vs Brasileirao_Matches 2019: same fixture, dates differ? One file has the *original* schedule date, the other the *actual played* date.\n2. BRFB: different date or different team order.\n3. Home/away swapped?\n\nLet me diagnose concretely. Also this confirms I need the \"preferred single source per season\" strategy for standings and general match listing (not just dedup by exact key). Better approach: for each (competition, season), pick the authoritative source = source with most matches? No — pick by priority list per competition:\n- BRASILEIRAO_A: Brasileirao_Matches (2012-2022), novo (2003-2011), BRFB (2023)\n- COPA_DO_BRASIL: Brazilian_Cup_Matches (2012-2021), BRFB (2022-2023)\n- LIBERTADORES: Libertadores_Matches only\n- B/C: BRFB only\n\nRather than hardcoding year ranges, rule: for each (competition, season), group matches by source; drop sources that are a strict SUBSET (~85%+) of a higher-priority source's set for that season. Simpler robust rule: order sources by priority; keep matches from the first source that covers that (competition, season); only fall back to lower-priority sources for fixtures NOT covered by the preferred source (identified by pairing+score, not date — because dates differ!).\n\nDedup v2: key on (competition, season, home_id, away_id, home_goals, away_goals) — fixture identity regardless of date. For 2019 Série A: Brasileirao_Matches has 380 fixtures; novo has same 380 fixtures (same scores!); BRFB too. Key without date → dedups correctly UNLESS the same pairing occurs twice in a season with the same score (possible in a 38-round league: teams play each other twice — home and away — so pairing (home,away) unique per season in a league ✓. In cups: two legs are home/away swapped ✓ distinct keys. Same-fixture same-score collisions: league — (home,away) unique ✓; cup replays rare ✓).\n\nBut wait — what about a cup pairing repeated with same score in same season? E.g., Copa do Brasil two legs: leg1 home A, leg2 home B — keys differ ✓. BRFB Copa do Brasil vs Brazilian_Cup: same fixtures ✓ dedup ✓.\n\nWhat about Libertadores group stage: teams play home and away ✓ distinct. Knockouts: two legs swapped ✓.\n\nSo dedup key WITHOUT date, but WITH score. Edge: date moved fixtures between sources — dedup still works ✓.\n\nRisk: legit distinct matches collapsing — e.g., friendly? not in data. Série C has 4-team groups? Série C format: teams meet multiple times per season! Série C (BRFB): ~2016+ format has groups of 4-5 where teams play each other TWICE home... within group stage, team A hosts team B once? Actually Série C first stage: 20 teams in 5 groups of 4, double round-robin → A hosts B once (2 meetings total, one each venue) ✓ keys distinct. Hmm wait double round robin = A@home vs B once, B@home vs A once ✓. Second stage knockouts two legs ✓. OK safe.\n\nBUT what about the same pairing, same score, same venue occurring twice in a season legitimately? Série C knockout + group? Possible in theory: group stage A 1-0 B and knockout A 1-0 B — same season, same home, same score → FALSE dedup. Rare; and only BRFB (single source for Série C anyway — dedup only matters across sources... but my dedup also removes within-source duplicates. Restrict within-source dedup? A source legitimately could have A 1-0 B twice. Hmm — safer: dedup key (competition, season, home_id, away_id, home_goals, away_goals, source_priority_class)? No wait — dedup ONLY across sources: key + \"first source wins\" only when sources differ. Within same source, keep everything. Let me implement: seen map key → source; if key seen AND current source != recorded source → skip; if same source → keep (legit repeat).\n\nHmm, but within-source the key can't repeat EXCEPT legit repeats (Série C scenario) — keep them. Across-source repeats are dupes unless legit... e.g., Brazilian_Cup vs BRFB Copa do Brasil 2015: same fixture, same score → dedup ✓ desired.\n\nEdge risk: BRFB Copa do Brasil fixture with same pairing+score as a DIFFERENT real fixture in Brazilian_Cup (e.g. two cup ties between same teams same score, different rounds — Copa do Brasil CAN have same pairing in different rounds? No — knockout, teams eliminated. Two legs = swapped venues ✓).\n\nOK dedup v2: key = (competition, season, home_id, away_id, hg, ag); skip if key seen from a DIFFERENT source; keep if same source repeat. Sources ordered by authority, so first occurrence is authoritative. Also date=None matches: BRFB has dates; Libertadores NA row skipped. Fixture identity with None scores: key (..., None, None) — multiple unplayed fixtures between same teams? Rare; fine.\n\nAlso — the 2023 Série A (BRFB only): unique ✓. 2012-2019 Série A: 3 sources dedup to Brasileirao_Matches ✓. 2020-2022: Brasileirao_Matches + BRFB → dedup ✓. 2003-2011: novo only ✓. Copa do Brasil 2012-2021: Brazilian_Cup (+BRFB 2014-2021) ✓; 2022-2023: BRFB ✓.\n\nLet me diagnose the 2019 dupes first to confirm the date-mismatch hypothesis, then implement dedup v2.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b465cb0001KLkfGjLZCB5HVM","sessionID":"ses_fa4ccfc0bffexSFu2vIRQjobrF","messageID":"msg_05b45ac92001Tl5qdL5T2crU85"}}
