{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788238235359,"sessionID":"ses_fa4ccfc0bffexSFu2vIRQjobrF","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_4614ce9dd2d94b7a8dee50fc","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"./venv/bin/python << 'EOF'\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.loaders import load_all\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.service import SoccerService\nsvc = SoccerService(load_all('data/kaggle'))\n\nst = svc.standings(\"serie a\", 2023)\nprint(\"2023 Serie A teams:\", len(st.table), \"| total played:\", sum(r.matches for r in st.table)//2)\nfor r in st.table[:4]:\n    print(f\"  {r.display}: {r.points}pts {r.wins}W {r.draws}D {r.losses}L\")\nprint(\"...\")\nfor r in st.table[-4:]:\n    print(f\"  {r.display}: {r.points}pts {r.wins}W {r.draws}D {r.losses}L\")\n\n# check unplayed count per season for brasileirao\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.models import BRASILEIRAO_A\nunplayed = Counter(); total = Counter()\nfor m in svc.data.matches:\n    if m.competition == BRASILEIRAO_A and m.source == svc.primary_source(BRASILEIRAO_A, m.season):\n        total[m.season] += 1\n        if not m.played(): unplayed[m.season] += 1\nprint(\"unplayed per season:\", {k: v for k, v in sorted(unplayed.items())})\nprint(\"totals:\", dict(sorted(total.items())))\nEOF"},"output":"2023 Serie A teams: 20 | total played: 377\n  Grêmio: 68pts 21W 5D 12L\n  Palmeiras: 67pts 19W 10D 8L\n  Atlético Mineiro: 66pts 19W 9D 10L\n  Flamengo: 66pts 19W 9D 10L\n...\n  Vasco da Gama: 42pts 11W 9D 17L\n  Goiás: 39pts 9W 12D 17L\n  Coritiba: 30pts 8W 6D 23L\n  América Mineiro: 24pts 5W 9D 24L\nunplayed per season: {2016: 1, 2022: 81}\ntotals: {2003: 552, 2004: 552, 2005: 462, 2006: 380, 2007: 380, 2008: 380, 2009: 380, 2010: 380, 2011: 380, 2012: 380, 2013: 380, 2014: 380, 2015: 380, 2016: 380, 2017: 380, 2018: 380, 2019: 380, 2020: 380, 2021: 212, 2022: 380, 2023: 377}\n","metadata":{"output":"2023 Serie A teams: 20 | total played: 377\n  Grêmio: 68pts 21W 5D 12L\n  Palmeiras: 67pts 19W 10D 8L\n  Atlético Mineiro: 66pts 19W 9D 10L\n  Flamengo: 66pts 19W 9D 10L\n...\n  Vasco da Gama: 42pts 11W 9D 17L\n  Goiás: 39pts 9W 12D 17L\n  Coritiba: 30pts 8W 6D 23L\n  América Mineiro: 24pts 5W 9D 24L\nunplayed per season: {2016: 1, 2022: 81}\ntotals: {2003: 552, 2004: 552, 2005: 462, 2006: 380, 2007: 380, 2008: 380, 2009: 380, 2010: 380, 2011: 380, 2012: 380, 2013: 380, 2014: 380, 2015: 380, 2016: 380, 2017: 380, 2018: 380, 2019: 380, 2020: 380, 2021: 212, 2022: 380, 2023: 377}\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"./venv/bin/python << 'EOF'\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.loaders import load_all\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.service import SoccerService\nsvc = SoccerService(load_all('data/kaggle'))\n\nst = svc.standings(\"serie a\", 2023)\nprint(\"2023 Serie A teams:\", len(st.table), \"| total played:\", sum(r.matches for r in st.table)//2)\nfor r in st.table[:4]:\n    print(f\"  {r.display}: {r.points}pts {r.wins}W {r.draws}D {r.losses}L\")\nprint(\"...\")\nfor r in st.table[-4:]:\n    print(f\"  {r.display}: {r.points}pts {r.wins}W {r.draws}D {r.losses}L\")\n\n# check unplayed count per season for brasileirao\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.models import BRASILEIRAO_A\nunplayed = Counter(); total = Counter()\nfor m in svc.data.matches:\n    if m.competition == BRASILEIRAO_A and m.source == svc.primary_source(BRASILEIRAO_A, m.season):\n        total[m.season] += 1\n        if not m.played(): unplayed[m.season] += 1\nprint(\"unplayed per season:\", {k: v for k, v in sorted(unplayed.items())})\nprint(\"totals:\", dict(sorted(total.items())))\nEOF","time":{"start":1788238235329,"end":1788238235358}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Found it! The last 4 Corinthians home matches in 2022 have `?-?` — missing scores! The raw CSV has empty home_goal/away_goal for some late-2022 matches (the dataset was captured before the season ended — rounds 35-38 incomplete). My `played()` filter excludes them from records, giving 15 instead of 19.\n\nWait — but the file has all 380 rows for 2022 with 10 per round... with 40 matches unplayed (rounds 35-38 × 10 = 40). So `total 2022 rows: 380` includes unplayed fixtures. My team_record only counts PLAYED matches ✓ correct behavior (you can't count a W/D/L for an unplayed game). So \"Corinthians home record in 2022\" = 15 PLAYED matches (10W 4D 1L) — CORRECT for this dataset! The spec example (19 matches, 11W 5D 3L) is illustrative, not real data.\n\nHmm interesting — but then `standings(\"brasileirao\", 2022)` will be a partial table (everyone played 34 games). That's data reality — the standings tool should probably NOTE when a season looks incomplete. Nice touch: add a note when total matches < expected for a 20-team double round-robin? Simpler: report \"N matches included\" in standings output. Let me add match count to standings format. Also for the champion of 2022 — Palmeiras won 2022 in reality and had most points after 34 rounds? The table after 34 rounds: Palmeiras was leading? Actually the dataset stops mid-season... no wait — 2022 season DID end (Palmeiras champion). The dataset just didn't record the last 4 rounds. Hmm, wait: did it? Let me check how many played matches 2022 has: 380-40=340. Rounds 1-34 complete. So standings computed from 34 rounds.\n\nFor the test, I'll assert standings on 2019 (complete season, 380 played) instead of 2022. And 2023 (BRFB 377 matches — complete-ish: 2023 had 380... 377 < 380, maybe 3 unplayed or missing). I'll check.\n\nAlso — the unplayed matches have `?-?` scores in listings. Fine — listings show scheduled fixtures without scores. Actually nice for \"match schedules and results\" (competition queries requirement: \"Match schedules and results\").\n\nNow fix the remaining issues:\n1. `champion()` cup finals formatting bug (both legs on one line).\n2. Copa do Brasil finals fallback when no round data (2022-2023 BRFB): last matches heuristic.\n3. Add match count note to standings (completeness transparency).\n\nAlso check 2023 Série A: BRFB 377 — playable? Let me check played count. And check what `standings(\"serie a\", 2023)` gives — champion? Real 2023 champion: Palmeiras. Let me verify from data.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b4e037a001tUlyjKUD3Hs5RZ","sessionID":"ses_fa4ccfc0bffexSFu2vIRQjobrF","messageID":"msg_05b4da0780017MQpHx0CY46t4w"}}
