{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788238258036,"sessionID":"ses_fa4ccfc0bffexSFu2vIRQjobrF","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_423b848329ef479583d68fb1","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"./venv/bin/python << 'EOF'\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.loaders import load_all\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.models import BRASILEIRAO_A, COPA_DO_BRASIL\ndata = load_all('data/kaggle')\nfor season in [2021, 2016]:\n    print(season, data.source_counts_by_season.get((BRASILEIRAO_A, season)))\nprint(\"Cup 2022/2023:\", data.source_counts_by_season.get((COPA_DO_BRASIL, 2022)), data.source_counts_by_season.get((COPA_DO_BRASIL, 2023)))\n# cup finals rounds per season\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nmx = defaultdict(int)\nfor m in data.matches:\n    if m.competition == COPA_DO_BRASIL and m.round_no:\n        try: r = int(m.round_no)\n        except ValueError: continue\n        mx[m.season] = max(mx[m.season], r)\nprint(\"max cup round per season:\", dict(sorted(mx.items())))\nEOF"},"output":"2021 {'Brasileirao_Matches.csv': 380, 'BR-Football-Dataset.csv': 491}\n2016 {'Brasileirao_Matches.csv': 380, 'novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv': 380, 'BR-Football-Dataset.csv': 379}\nCup 2022/2023: {'BR-Football-Dataset.csv': 117} {'BR-Football-Dataset.csv': 116}\nmax cup round per season: {2012: 6, 2013: 8, 2014: 8, 2015: 8, 2016: 7, 2017: 8, 2018: 8, 2019: 8, 2020: 8, 2021: 4}\n","metadata":{"output":"2021 {'Brasileirao_Matches.csv': 380, 'BR-Football-Dataset.csv': 491}\n2016 {'Brasileirao_Matches.csv': 380, 'novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv': 380, 'BR-Football-Dataset.csv': 379}\nCup 2022/2023: {'BR-Football-Dataset.csv': 117} {'BR-Football-Dataset.csv': 116}\nmax cup round per season: {2012: 6, 2013: 8, 2014: 8, 2015: 8, 2016: 7, 2017: 8, 2018: 8, 2019: 8, 2020: 8, 2021: 4}\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"./venv/bin/python << 'EOF'\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.loaders import load_all\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.models import BRASILEIRAO_A, COPA_DO_BRASIL\ndata = load_all('data/kaggle')\nfor season in [2021, 2016]:\n    print(season, data.source_counts_by_season.get((BRASILEIRAO_A, season)))\nprint(\"Cup 2022/2023:\", data.source_counts_by_season.get((COPA_DO_BRASIL, 2022)), data.source_counts_by_season.get((COPA_DO_BRASIL, 2023)))\n# cup finals rounds per season\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nmx = defaultdict(int)\nfor m in data.matches:\n    if m.competition == COPA_DO_BRASIL and m.round_no:\n        try: r = int(m.round_no)\n        except ValueError: continue\n        mx[m.season] = max(mx[m.season], r)\nprint(\"max cup round per season:\", dict(sorted(mx.items())))\nEOF","time":{"start":1788238258014,"end":1788238258034}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Interesting findings:\n- 2023 Série A: 377/380 played, Grêmio 68 > Palmeiras 67 — but real 2023 champion was Palmeiras (70 pts). The BRFB data is slightly off/incomplete. Data reality — the tool reports what's in the data. Actually wait: 2023 real standings: Palmeiras 70, Grêmio 68, Atlético 66...? Palmeiras 2023: 70 pts (21W 7D 10L? no). BRFB says Grêmio 21W 5D 12L = 68. Real Grêmio 2023: 68 pts ✓ correct. Real Palmeiras 2023: 70 pts (23W? no — 21W 7D 10L=70). BRFB has Palmeiras 19W 10D 8L = 67 → missing/differing 3 matches (377 vs 380). So the 2023 data is 3 matches short and slightly wrong. It's the only 2023 source — fine, we report data faithfully. For tests I'll use 2019 (clean, matches spec exactly).\n\n- 2021: only 212/380 in primary source?? Brasileirao_Matches 2021 incomplete (dataset captured mid-2021?). Let me check raw counts: earlier source_row_counts showed Brasileirao_Matches 4180 total rows for 2012-2022. Per-season: 2021: 212? Hmm — earlier `source_counts_by_season` for (Série A, 2021): Brasileirao_Matches ? + BRFB ? Let me check: 2021 totals from primary = 212. If Brasileirao_Matches 2021 has 212 and BRFB 2021 has ~380, then max-count picks BRFB (380)! But the printout says primary total for 2021 = 