1-12-12 Atletico Mineiro 4.0 - 0.0 Athletico Paranaense\n   2021-12-16 Athletico Paranaense 1.0 - 2.0 Atletico Mineiro\nBRFB 2022 cup last 2:\n   2022-10-13 Corinthians 0.0 - 0.0 Flamengo\n   2022-10-20 Flamengo 1.0 - 1.0 Corinthians\nBRFB 2023 cup last 2:\n   2023-09-17 Flamengo 0.0 - 1.0 Sao Paulo\n   2023-09-24 Sao Paulo 1.0 - 1.0 Flamengo\n","metadata":{"output":"Brazilian_Cup 2021 last 3:\n   2021-08-05 16:00:00 Crb - AL NA - NA Fortaleza - CE round 4\n   2021-08-05 19:15:00 Atlético - GO NA - NA Athletico Paranaense - PR round 4\n   2021-08-05 21:30:00 Abc - RN NA - NA Flamengo - RJ round 4\nBRFB 2021 last 4:\n   2021-10-28 Fortaleza FC 1.0 - 2.0 Atletico Mineiro\n   2021-10-28 Flamengo 0.0 - 3.0 Athletico Paranaense\n   2021-12-12 Atletico Mineiro 4.0 - 0.0 Athletico Paranaense\n   2021-12-16 Athletico Paranaense 1.0 - 2.0 Atletico Mineiro\nBRFB 2022 cup last 2:\n   2022-10-13 Corinthians 0.0 - 0.0 Flamengo\n   2022-10-20 Flamengo 1.0 - 1.0 Corinthians\nBRFB 2023 cup last 2:\n   2023-09-17 Flamengo 0.0 - 1.0 Sao Paulo\n   2023-09-24 Sao Paulo 1.0 - 1.0 Flamengo\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"./venv/bin/python << 'EOF'\nimport csv\n# Latest Copa do Brasil matches in 2021 from each source\nrows1 = []\nwith open('data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    for row in csv.DictReader(f):\n        if row['season'] == '2021': rows1.append(row)\nrows1.sort(key=lambda r: r['datetime'])\nprint(\"Brazilian_Cup 2021 last 3:\")\nfor r in rows1[-3:]: print(\"  \", r['datetime'], r['home_team'], r['home_goal'], '-', r['away_goal'], r['away_team'], \"round\", r['round'])\n\nrows2 = []\nwith open('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    for row in csv.DictReader(f):\n        if row['tournament'] == 'Copa do Brasil' and row['date'].startswith('2021'): rows2.append(row)\nrows2.sort(key=lambda r: r['date'])\nprint(\"BRFB 2021 last 4:\")\nfor r in rows2[-4:]: print(\"  \", r['date'], r['home'], r['home_goal'], '-', r['away_goal'], r['away'])\n\n# 2022 & 2023 cup last matches (BRFB only)\nfor yr in ('2022', '2023'):\n    rows = []\n    with open('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        for row in csv.DictReader(f):\n            if row['tournament'] == 'Copa do Brasil' and row['date'].startswith(yr): rows.append(row)\n    rows.sort(key=lambda r: r['date'])\n    print(f\"BRFB {yr} cup last 2:\")\n    for r in rows[-2:]: print(\"  \", r['date'], r['home'], r['home_goal'], '-', r['away_goal'], r['away'])\nEOF","time":{"start":1788238355160,"end":1788238355163}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Cup data analysis:\n- 2012: rounds 1-6, round 6 = 2 matches (two-legged final) ✓\n- 2013-2015: rounds up to 8, round 8 = 2 matches (final, two legs) ✓\n- 2016: rounds 1-7, round 7 = 2 matches ✓ (final)\n- 2017-2020: rounds up to 8, round 8 = 2 ✓\n- 2021: rounds 1-4 ONLY — truncated (real 2021 final: Atlético-MG vs Athletico-PR). The dataset stops at round 4 (round of 16?). 108 matches. So NO finals for 2021 in this file. BRFB 2021 Copa do Brasil has 111 matches — does it include later rounds? BRFB has no round info, but might include the final matches by date! The 2021 cup final was Dec 2021 (Athletico-PR? no — 2021 final: Atlético-MG beat Athletico-PR? Yes, Dec 2021). BRFB might contain those matches. \n\nSo for Copa do Brasil 2021: Brazilian_Cup (priority) has 108 matches but NO final; BRFB has 111. If I use priority-first (Brazilian_Cup), finals → max round 4 = 16 matches → WRONG \"finals\".\n\nHmm. This is getting complicated. Options for `finals(\"Copa do Brasil\", season)`:\n- Gather final-stage matches across the DEDUPED set (not primary): matches with round data → max round per season; PLUS for seasons where max round < 5 (truncated: 2021), fall back to last-N-by-date from the deduped set.\n- For 2022/2023 (BRFB only, no rounds): last-N-by-date fallback.\n\nThe \"last-N-by-date\" heuristic: take the latest 2 matches of the season (two-legged finals through 2023); if both involve the same 2 teams → two-legged final; if the latest match is single and the pairing of the last two differ → single final.\n\nActually — cleanest: `finals()` uses deduped all-source matches for the season. Identify candidates:\n1. Matches WITH round data: max round group (if that round has ≤ 4 matches — sanity: a \"final round\" has 1-2 matches (+maybe 3rd place? no)). If max-round group has ≤4 matches → finals ✓ (2012-2020 ✓).\n2. Else (2021: max round 4 has 16 matches → not finals; 2022/2023: no round data) → fallback: last matches by date: take latest date d1; matches on d1; plus if the second-latest date's matches pair the same teams → those too. Simplify: take the last 2 chronological PLAYED matches; if they share the same team pair → 2-legged final; else just the last 1.\n\nFor 2021 with BRFB present: last 2 matches by date across deduped sources → if BRFB includes the real final (Atlético-MG x Athletico-PR Dec 2021 two legs Nov 27? and Dec 1?) hmm — actually 2021 final was single?? No: 2021 Copa do Brasil final = two legs? Hmm, 2021: Athletico-PR vs Atlético-MG... I believe two-legged (last two-legged era; single-match finals started 2024? no — 2023 was two-legged: Flamengo x São Paulo. Single from... doesn't matter!). The heuristic handles both.\n\nBut also for `champion(\"Copa do Brasil\", 2021)` — the finals heuristic picks last-2-by-date — but if BRFB 2021 cup data is ALSO truncated before the final, we'd wrongly crown a semifinalist. Let me check BRFB 2021 cup dates: what's the latest 2021 cup match in BRFB?\n\nAlso — the max-round rule: is round 8 always the final? 2013: round 8 = 2 matches ✓ final two legs. 2017-2020 ✓. So for seasons 2012-2020, finals = max-round matches (2 matches each) ✓ verified counts.\n\nFor 2021: let me check latest dates in both sources.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b4fda76001Lll7eT2llT0Yff","sessionID":"ses_fa4ccfc0bffexSFu2vIRQjobrF","message