s: 2.4ms\n2022 standings tail: Note: based on 299 played matches in the dataset (a complete 20-team season has 380); later rounds were not recorded.\nlib avg goals: 2.55 | matches: 1253\nfla-flu total: 46 | shown: 30\n","metadata":{"output":"last Fla-Cor: 2023-10-08 Corinthians 1-1 Flamengo | Brasileirão Série A\ntotal Fla-Cor: 50\ncup finals count all seasons: 2\nlib finals count: 14\nsearch: 0.8ms | standings: 0.6ms | stats: 2.4ms\n2022 standings tail: Note: based on 299 played matches in the dataset (a complete 20-team season has 380); later rounds were not recorded.\nlib avg goals: 2.55 | matches: 1253\nfla-flu total: 46 | shown: 30\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"./venv/bin/python << 'EOF'\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.loaders import load_all\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.service import SoccerService\nsvc = SoccerService(load_all('data/kaggle'))\n\n# last Flamengo vs Corinthians match\nres = svc.search_matches(team=\"Flamengo\", opponent=\"Corinthians\", limit=1)\nfor m in res.matches: print(\"last Fla-Cor:\", m.date_str(), m.home_display, m.score_str(), m.away_display, \"|\", m.competition)\nprint(\"total Fla-Cor:\", res.total)\n\n# Copa do Brasil finals list all seasons\nf = svc.finals(\"Copa do Brasil\")\nprint(\"cup finals count all seasons:\", len(f))\n\n# Libertadores finals all seasons\nf = svc.finals(\"Libertadores\")\nprint(\"lib finals count:\", len(f))\n\n# performance\nimport time\nt0=time.time(); svc.search_matches(team=\"Flamengo\"); t1=time.time()\nsvc.standings(\"brasileirao\", 2019); t2=time.time()\nsvc.competition_stats(\"brasileirao\"); t3=time.time()\nprint(f\"search: {(t1-t0)*1000:.1f}ms | standings: {(t2-t1)*1000:.1f}ms | stats: {(t3-t2)*1000:.1f}ms\")\n\n# unplayed 2022 note: standings 2022 note text\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp import formatting as fmt\nout = fmt.format_standings(svc.standings(\"brasileirao\", 2022))\nprint(\"2022 standings tail:\", out.split(\"\\n\")[-1])\n\n# avg goals Libertadores\ns = svc.competition_stats(\"libertadores\")\nprint(\"lib avg goals:\", s.avg_goals, \"| matches:\", s.matches)\n\n# search_matches limit behavior: fla-flu total\nres = svc.search_matches(team=\"Flamengo\", opponent=\"Fluminense\")\nprint(\"fla-flu total:\", res.total, \"| shown:\", len(res.matches))\nEOF","time":{"start":1788238671047,"end":1788238671067}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The MCP server works end-to-end with 20 tools. Now write the BDD GWT test suite. Structure:\n\ntests/conftest.py:\n- `service` session fixture (loads real data once)\n- `mcp` fixtures: event loop + server + client session (session-scoped; need anyio/asyncio fixture — pytest with asyncio? anyio plugin is a dependency of mcp. pytest-anyio? mcp depends on anyio; the anyio pytest plugin ships with anyio itself (anyio.pytest_plugin). Check if anyio's pytest plugin is available. I'll use `pytest.mark.anyio` with an `anyio_backend` fixture = \"asyncio\". Or write a module-scoped sync fixture that runs asyncio.run to create a persistent client... simpler: make the MCP test class use `@pytest.mark.anyio` with the fixture returning the session. Let me check anyio pytest plugin availability in the venv.\n\nTest files (BDD GWT structure with Gherkin docstrings per the spec's Testing Approach):\n1. tests/test_normalizer.py — team name variations\n2. tests/test_loaders.py — all 6 files load, dedup, dates, UTF-8\n3. tests/test_match_queries.py\n4. tests/test_team_queries.py\n5. tests/test_player_queries.py\n6. tests/test_competition_queries.py\n7. tests/test_statistics.py\n8. tests/test_server.py — MCP integration (in-memory client)\n9. tests/test_sample_questions.py — the 20+ sample questions coverage (spec: \"At least 20 sample questions can be answered\") — I'll write ~24 GWT scenarios mapping each spec question to a tool call.\n\nAssertions use the ground truth established above:\n- 2019 Série A: Flamengo 90pts 28W 6D 4L; Santos 2nd (22W); 20 teams; 380 matches\n- Libertadores 2019 champion Flamengo 2-1 River Plate\n- Copa do Brasil 2023 champion São Paulo (agg 2-1)\n- h2h Fla-Flu: Flamengo 18 wins, Fluminense 15, 13 draws, 46 matches\n- Corinthians home 2022 Série A: 15 played (10W 4D 1L, GF21 GA7)\n- Palmeiras overview: 939 matches 445W 236D 258L; Série A seasons 2004-2023\n- derbies 2023: 23\n- biggest wins: São Paulo 9-1 4 de Julho (Copa do Brasil 2021-06-08)\n- Série A all-time avg goals 2.56 (round to 2), home win rate 49.6%\n- best away all-time min 50: Flamengo 34.8%\n- 2020 relegated: Botafogo, Coritiba, Goiás, Vasco\n- Libertadores 2019 semis: Flamengo 5-0 Grêmio\n- Brazilian players: 827; Neymar 92 top; Casemiro/Coutinho 88\n- Santos squad: 20 players\n- search date range Palmeiras 2023-08/09: 7 matches\n- FIFA 827 Brazilian players\n\nWait — one more check: Brazilian players count 827 (computed earlier via Nationality=='Brazil'). ✓\n\nAlso \"Flamengo last played Corinthians\" (most recent match): search with team+opponent sorted desc → last match = ? The search returns `shown = selected[-limit:]` — with limit=30 default, we get the LAST 30 chronologically (most recent). For \"when did Flamengo last play Corinthians\" the LLM would call search_matches(team=Flamengo, opponent=Corinthians, limit=1) → gets the most recent ✓ (selected[-1:] = latest). Good design. Let me verify what the latest Fla-Cor match is: need ground truth. Flamengo x Corinthians in 2023 Série A (BRFB): check quickly in the test itself as \">= 2023-01-01\" assertion, or compute now for exact value.\n\nLet me also double check performance requirement with timing test — spec: simple < 2s, aggregate < 5s. I'll add a test asserting response times with generous margins (queries are ms-fast after load; load itself ~0.8s excluded... but the spec says \"Simple lookups respond in < 2 seconds\" — including load? Load 0.8s + query ms < 2s ✓. I'll time from cold service creation? That'd re-load data (~0.8s) — acceptable in one test.)\n\nLet me check the last Flamengo-Corinthians match and a couple more ground truths, then write tests.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b54a983001Vz1OWSVyTJAuTl","sessionID":"ses_fa4ccfc0bffexSFu2vIRQjobrF","messageID":"msg_05b543727001WgpKl8isrDmqC8"}}
