ense-PI? Fluminense-RJ vs... maybe \"Fluminense-PI\" or \"Fluminense-BA\" in Copa do Brasil small clubs). So bare \"Fluminense\" (FIFA/Libertadores/BRFB) → default state... `_default_state_for(\"fluminense\")` → frequency → \"rj\" presumably → \"fluminense-rj\"; while \"Fluminense-RJ\" (Brasileirao_Matches suffixed) → \"fluminense-rj\" — hmm but the failure shows BOTH \"fluminense-rj\" AND \"fluminense\" ids exist. So the FINALIZE logic produced both? Let me think: if base \"fluminense\" has states {rj, X} → ambiguous → suffixed ids \"fluminense-rj\" and \"fluminense-X\"; bare \"Fluminense\" → default → \"fluminense-rj\". Then where does bare id \"fluminense\" come from?? The failing match has home/away ids {flamengo-rj, fluminense-rj} on one match and {flamengo-rj, fluminense}... on another? The set comparison failed because across matches, BOTH ids appear.\n\nWhere does id \"fluminense\" come from? A raw name that parses to base \"fluminense\" with NO state... if base is ambiguous, finalize maps bare → default state. UNLESS the bare provisional id was never registered in `_by_base[base][None]`... it would be. Hmm — OR the FIFA club \"Fluminense\" registered pre-finalize ✓ should map to default state too...\n\nWait — actually let me check: is \"fluminense\" ambiguous at all? Let me look for Fluminense variants with other states. If NOT ambiguous (only rj), then finalize strips → canonical \"fluminense\" for ALL — but then where does \"fluminense-rj\" come from?! The match set shows 'fluminense-rj' present. So suffixed ids exist → ambiguous → bare → default. The observed ids suggest BOTH mappings exist in the data — meaning finalize produced inconsistent results.\n\nAH WAIT — I bet the bug is the fixture display names on Match were computed with `registry.display(team_id)` where display falls back to `team_id.title()` for unknown ids... but that's cosmetic.\n\nLet me think about `_canonical_from_parsed` (used by resolve) vs finalize remap. The test uses search_matches which uses resolve_team(\"Fluminense\") → `_canonical_from_parsed` → parsed base \"fluminense\", no state → ambiguous? If yes → default → \"fluminense-rj\". The MATCH ids come from finalize remap: \"Fluminense\" bare → remap → \"fluminense-rj\"; \"Fluminense-RJ\" → \"fluminense-rj\". So match ids should all be \"fluminense-rj\"... unless NOT ambiguous: finalize: base states {rj} only → unambiguous → ALL → \"fluminense\". Then match ids all \"fluminense\", and resolve → \"fluminense\". But the failure shows \"fluminense-rj\" in matches! Contradiction → some raw Fluminense variant produced a DIFFERENT provisional id that remapped to \"fluminense-rj\" while others → \"fluminense\"...\n\nHmm wait — maybe there IS a second Fluminense club (like \"Fluminense-PI\"), making base ambiguous. Then: bare \"Fluminense\" → \"fluminense-rj\" (default). \"Fluminense-RJ\" → \"fluminense-rj\". So ids in matches: \"fluminense-rj\" only. But failure shows \"fluminense\" also present! Where from?!\n\nOH WAIT. I see it. Look at finalize:\n\n```python\nfor base, states in self._by_base.items():\n    ambiguous = base in self._ambiguous_bases\n    ...\n    if not ambiguous:\n        canonical = base\n        for state, pid in states.items():\n            if state and not state.startswith(\"foreign:\"):\n                remap[pid] = canonical\n```\n\nFor ambiguous bases, the loop maps suffixed pids AND bare pid. But `_ambiguous_bases` is computed FIRST from `_by_base` — fine.\n\nHmm, but what about the FIFA registration phase: FIFA \"Fluminense\" → provisional \"fluminense\" (bare). If match data also has \"Fluminense-RJ\" (provisional \"fluminense-rj\") and, say, \"Fluminense-PI\"... then ambiguous → bare → default rj ✓.\n\nSo both map to \"fluminense-rj\". Where would \"fluminense\" id appear in matches?! Let me actually DEBUG rather than theorize — check which raw names map to \"fluminense\" vs \"fluminense-rj\".\n\nActually — hold on. The earlier h2h test PASSED with `{\"flamengo-rj\"