{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788239151873,"sessionID":"ses_fa4ccfc0bffexSFu2vIRQjobrF","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_42006235e28f4479942eac07","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"./venv/bin/python << 'EOF'\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.loaders import load_all\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.models import BRASILEIRAO_A\nfrom collections import Counter\ndata = load_all('data/kaggle')\n\n# Deduped Série A per source\nc = Counter(m.source for m in data.matches if m.competition == BRASILEIRAO_A)\nprint(\"Série A deduped per source:\", dict(c))\n\n# fluminense ids present\nfl = Counter()\nfor m in data.matches:\n    for tid in (m.home_id, m.away_id):\n        if 'fluminense' in tid: fl[tid] += 1\nprint(\"fluminense ids in matches:\", dict(fl))\n\n# fifa clubs bridged to santos-sp\nprint(\"fifa clubs santos-sp:\", data.fifa_clubs_by_team.get('santos-sp'))\nprint(\"fifa clubs fluminense*:\", {k: v for k, v in data.fifa_clubs_by_team.items() if 'fluminense' in k})\n\n# registry internals for fluminense\nreg = data.registry\nprint(\"ambiguous?\", 'fluminense' in reg._ambiguous_bases)\nprint(\"by_base fluminense:\", reg._by_base.get('fluminense'))\nprint(\"remap entries for fluminense pids:\", {pid: r for pid, r in reg._remap.items() if 'fluminense' in pid})\nEOF"},"output":"Série A deduped per source: {'Brasileirao_Matches.csv': 4180, 'novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv': 3847, 'BR-Football-Dataset.csv': 847}\nfluminense ids in matches: {'fluminense-rj': 940, 'fluminense de feira': 3, 'fluminense-pi': 3}\nfifa clubs santos-sp: ['Santos']\nfifa clubs fluminense*: {'fluminense-rj': ['Fluminense']}\nambiguous? True\nby_base fluminense: {'rj': 'fluminense-rj', None: 'fluminense', 'pi': 'fluminense-pi'}\nremap entries for fluminense pids: {'fluminense-rj': 'fluminense-rj', 'fluminense-pi': 'fluminense-pi', 'fluminense': 'fluminense-rj', 'fluminense de feira-ba': 'fluminense de feira', 'fluminense de feira': 'fluminense de feira'}\n","metadata":{"output":"Série A deduped per source: {'Brasileirao_Matches.csv': 4180, 'novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv': 3847, 'BR-Football-Dataset.csv': 847}\nfluminense ids in matches: {'fluminense-rj': 940, 'fluminense de feira': 3, 'fluminense-pi': 3}\nfifa clubs santos-sp: ['Santos']\nfifa clubs fluminense*: {'fluminense-rj': ['Fluminense']}\nambiguous? True\nby_base fluminense: {'rj': 'fluminense-rj', None: 'fluminense', 'pi': 'fluminense-pi'}\nremap entries for fluminense pids: {'fluminense-rj': 'fluminense-rj', 'fluminense-pi': 'fluminense-pi', 'fluminense': 'fluminense-rj', 'fluminense de feira-ba': 'fluminense de feira', 'fluminense de feira': 'fluminense de feira'}\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"./venv/bin/python << 'EOF'\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.loaders import load_all\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.models import BRASILEIRAO_A\nfrom collections import Counter\ndata = load_all('data/kaggle')\n\n# Deduped Série A per source\nc = Counter(m.source for m in data.matches if m.competition == BRASILEIRAO_A)\nprint(\"Série A deduped per source:\", dict(c))\n\n# fluminense ids present\nfl = Counter()\nfor m in data.matches:\n    for tid in (m.home_id, m.away_id):\n        if 'fluminense' in tid: fl[tid] += 1\nprint(\"fluminense ids in matches:\", dict(fl))\n\n# fifa clubs bridged to santos-sp\nprint(\"fifa clubs santos-sp:\", data.fifa_clubs_by_team.get('santos-sp'))\nprint(\"fifa clubs fluminense*:\", {k: v for k, v in data.fifa_clubs_by_team.items() if 'fluminense' in k})\n\n# registry internals for fluminense\nreg = data.registry\nprint(\"ambiguous?\", 'fluminense' in reg._ambiguous_bases)\nprint(\"by_base fluminense:\", reg._by_base.get('fluminense'))\nprint(\"remap entries for fluminense pids:\", {pid: r for pid, r in reg._remap.items() if 'fluminense' in pid})\nEOF","time":{"start":1788239151850,"end":1788239151871}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now I understand the failures. Key insight: **state pollution across tests in the same session!** The stats test shows 9184 matches vs 8868 from my earlier probe — MORE matches. And Santos squad has 46 players vs 20. And \"fluminense-rj\" vs \"fluminense\".\n\nWait — 9184 > 8868? competition_stats counts PLAYED matches in the DEDUPED set (comp filter, no season). My probe earlier gave 8868... but the probe ran BEFORE my `primary_source` change? No — stats don't use primary_source with season=None... Hmm wait, actually: `_aggregation_matches(comp, None)` — comp given, season None → `result = [m for m in self.data.matches if m.competition == comp]` — deduped set. Same as before. 9184 vs 8868??\n\nOH WAIT. I bet the earlier probe was run BEFORE the `finals`/`champion` edit — no, those don't touch data... Hmm, 9184-8868 = 316. Santos squad 46 players vs 20 — 46 = 20 + 26?? TWO different FIFA club strings bridging to santos-sp! e.g. FIFA clubs \"Santos\" AND \"Santos Laguna\"?! If FIFA \"Santos Laguna\" (Mexican) maps to base \"santos laguna\" — distinct... UNLESS the alias/filler logic merges it! \"Santos Laguna\" → no state, base \"santos laguna\" — hmm that wouldn't merge with \"santos\".\n\nHold on — 46 = 20 (Santos) + 26 (Santos Laguna)? Santos Laguna has 26 players in FIFA ✓ plausible!! So `club_squad(\"Santos\")` → fifa_clubs_by_team[\"santos-sp\"] = [\"Santos\", \"Santos Laguna\"]?? How did Santos Laguna map to santos-sp? Through... resolve: parse \"Santos Laguna\" → base \"santos laguna\" — no. Through `_canonical_from_parsed`?? club_squad uses `resolve_team(club)` → resolve(\"Santos\") → ... → \"santos-sp\"; then fifa_clubs_by_team.get(\"santos-sp\") → should be [\"Santos\"] only...\n\nUNLESS fifa_clubs_by_team[\"santos-sp\"] contains both because during LOADING, FIFA club \"Santos Laguna\" registered provisional id \"santos laguna\"... remap... no.\n\nWAIT. What about \"Santos FC\"? Hmm. Or — the pollution theory: tests run in one process; conftest `data` fixture session-scoped — loaded ONCE. But `test_statistics.py::test_cold_load_and_query_under_budget` does a SECOND full `load_all` — module-level? No, inside the test — creates fresh data, doesn't touch shared.\n\nHmm hold on — `_load_players`... in the NEW loaders.py there's no post-finalize registration issue...\n\nLet me think about \"fluminense-rj\" vs \"fluminense\" again — the resolve(\"Fluminense-RJ\") returns \"fluminense-rj\" per the normalizer test failure. And matches contain both \"fluminense\" AND \"fluminense-rj\" ids. So finalize created BOTH canonical ids for Fluminense — the registry is internally inconsistent!\n\nHow? `register()` computes provisional ids and updates `_by_base`. finalize iterates `_by_base`. For base \"fluminense\" with states {None, \"rj\"}: ambiguous? brazilian_states = {\"rj\"} → len 1 → NOT ambiguous → remap: `for state, pid in states.items(): if state and not foreign: remap[pid] = canonical(\"fluminense\")`; `if bare_pid is not None: remap[bare_pid] = \"fluminense\"`. So both \"fluminense-rj\" (pid) and \"fluminense\" (pid) → \"fluminense\" ✓ consistent...\n\nUNLESS \"fluminense\" IS in _ambiguous_bases (states {rj, X} for some other Fluminense-X!). Then: suffixed → \"fluminense-rj\" and \"fluminense-X\"; bare → default → \"fluminense-rj\". All → suffixed ids. Then resolve(\"Fluminense-RJ\") → ambiguous → \"fluminense-rj\" ✓; and match ids ALL \"fluminense-rj\". But test_match_queries::test_flamengo_vs_fluminense PASSED with total 46 and pairing check FAILED showing matches contain \"fluminense\" too...\n\nWAIT — actually the pairing test shows left set has EXTRA \"fluminense-rj\" — meaning matches' ids = {flamengo-rj, fluminense} for MOST and some match has {flamengo-rj, fluminense-rj}?? The set assertion `== {\"flamengo-rj\", \"fluminense\"}` failed with extra item \"fluminense-rj\" — set union across loop. So SOME matches have fluminense-rj.\n\nWhich matches? Probably from a source whose Fluminense spelling maps to fluminense-rj while others → fluminense. Inconsistent remap → the SAME raw name maps differently at different times?? register is deterministic...\n\nOH WAIT!!! I see it!!! The module-level `_PROVISIONAL_CACHE` from the OLD loaders.py? No — removed in rewrite. Hmm.\n\nLet me look at the NEW loaders `canonical()`:\n\n```python\ndef canonical(raw_name: str) -> str:\n    pid = name_to_pid.get(raw_name)\n    if pid is None:\n        parsed = parse_name(raw_name)\n        pid = base-foreign / base-state / base\n    return remap.get(pid, pid)\n```\n\n`name_to_pid` was built during Phase 1 from match rows ✓ and FIFA clubs went to `club_to_pid` (separate). For match rows, canonical uses name_to_pid ✓ consistent.\n\nHmm... so where does inconsistency come from? Let me just debug concretely: load data, print fluminense-related provisional ids, their states, and final canonical ids + which matches carry which id.\n\nALSO — the 9184 vs 8868 discrepancy and Santos 46 players: maybe a SECOND club string bridges wrongly. Let me debug all three concretely. Actually — hmm, one BIG suspect: FIFA club registration BEFORE finalize. FIFA \"Fluminense\" → provisional \"fluminense\" (bare). Match data: \"Fluminense-RJ\" (Brasileirao_Matches) → provisional \"fluminense-rj\"; hist \"Fluminense\" (bare, from novo) → \"fluminense\". So base fluminense states: {None (from bare), \"rj\"} → 1 Brazilian state → unambiguous → both → \"fluminense\". All consistent → \"fluminense\". ✓ So where does \"fluminense-rj\" come from in MATCHES?!\n\nUnless... some OTHER raw name like \"Fluminense - RJ\"?? Same parse. \"Fluminense FC\"?? base \"fluminense\" bare. Hmm.\n\nDEBUG TIME. Also for Santos: print fifa_clubs_by_team[\"santos-sp\"], and for stats: count matches per source for Série A in the deduped set.\n\nActually — WAIT. I have a new suspicion: **the `service` fixture is fine, but tests run in the same process as test_server.py's `build_server(service)`** — which calls `get_service()`? No — build_server(service) injected. Hmm.\n\nBut WAIT — what about `brazilians_at_brazilian_clubs` or `variants` mutating?? No.\n\nHmm, actually — could the discrepancy be caused by TEST RUN ORDER + the `lru_cache` on `get_service()`? Not used by tests.\n\nLet me think about 9184 vs 8868 differently: is it possible my earlier probe was WRONG (before some loader change)? The probe ran after the fixture-identity dedup change... and before `primary_source` fix. `_aggregation_matches(comp, None)` doesn't involve primary_source. So stats should be identical. 9184-8868=316 extra PLAYED Série A matches in the deduped set. Did I change dedup between? NO. Did I change anything that affects the match list? ... the `finals` change? No.\n\nOH WAIT!!! I DID!!! In the FIX to `resolve_competition`... no. Hmm — Actually wait, did my earlier probe use `service.competition_stats(\"brasileirao\")`? YES — printed \"Statistics for Brasileirão Série A: Matches: 8868\". And now the same call gives 9184?!\n\nUnless the DATA fixture in tests differs — conftest DATA_DIR = Path(tests)/../data/kaggle — same directory.\n\nHmm hold on — 8868 was printed in the \"sweep\" run. Between then and now, what did I change in loaders/service? (1) dedupe key (fixture identity) — BEFORE the sweep. (2) primary_source priority-first — before sweep? The sweep ran after? Let me recount the timeline:\n1. dedup v2 (fixture identity) — implemented.\n2. smoke: 17491 matches, 6462 dupes removed.\n3. standings check 2019 → 90pts ✓ (used primary = Brasileirao_Matches via max-count).\n4. sweep run: \"stats Brasileirão all-time: 8868 matches\" ✓.\n5. primary_source → priority-first.\n6. finals/champion fixes.\n7. resolve_competition idempotency.\n8. Now tests: 9184.\n\nBetween 4 and 8, changes: primary_source (irrelevant for season=None), finals, champion, resolve_competition, standings-format note. None affect the deduped match list!!! Unless... conftest `data` fixture vs probe difference: the probe `load_all('data/kaggle')` relative path vs conftest absolute — same files.\n\nWAIT WAIT. Actually — maybe the tests aren't using the shared fixture! `test_statistics.py::TestCompetitionStats::test_brasileirao_all_time(self, service)` — service fixture — session-scoped, created once. Same as probe... UNLESS the async `mcp_session` fixture in test_server.py RE-CREATED the service?? `mcp_server` fixture depends on `service` — session-scoped, cached ✓.\n\nHmm — could pytest-asyncio/anyio load the module twice causing double registration?? load_all builds a FRESH registry per call — no shared state. And `data` fixture calls load_all ONCE per session.\n\nOK — actually, let me reconsider: is 9184 maybe correct and 8868 was wrong because the sweep ran with a STALE .pyc?? Unlikely.\n\nOR — test COLLECTION imports test_statistics.py which has `from tests.conftest import DATA_DIR` — imports conftest as module \"tests.conftest\" — pytest loads conftest as \"conftest\" too — two module instances, but fixtures still work. Not data-related.\n\nHmm, let me look at the numbers again: probe standings 2019 (complete) ✓, and total Série A DEDUPED played: sources: Brasileirao 4180 (2012-2022, some unplayed) + novo 6886 (2003-2019) + BRFB Serie A ~3400 (2014-2023). Raw total ≈ 14466. Dedup removed 6462 overall (all comps). Série A deduped ≈ 4180 + (novo 2003-2011 only: ~2300) + (BRFB 2023: 377) + residue ≈ 8868 ✓ probe. So 9184 = +316 more — as if BRFB Série A contributed MORE fixtures that weren't deduped... as if the DEDUP KEY CHANGED effectiveness...\n\nOH!!!! I FOUND IT!!! **`name_to_pid` mutation!** In loaders Phase 1:\n\n```python\nif raw not in name_to_pid:\n    name_to_pid[raw] = registry.register(raw)\nelse:\n    registry.register(raw)  # keep counting\n```\n\nregister returns provisional id — deterministic, fine...\n\nHmm no. Let me look at Phase 4 build: `builder(row, canonical, display_for, file_name)` — canonical(raw) — `name_to_pid.get(raw_name)` — raw key. **BUT the raw name from `row.get(\"home_team\",\"\")` is NOT STRIPPED in canonical's lookup!** `canonical` does `name_to_pid.get(raw_name)`