e normalizer test `test_fuzzy_and_unknown_input` expected \"fluminense\" — fix to \"fluminense-rj\".\n\nAlso note \"fluminense de feira\" → \"Fluminense de Feira-BA\" (Bahia club) correctly distinct.\n\nNow the Série A deduped per source: **novo kept 3847!** That's wrong — novo 2012-2019 should be deduped against Brasileirao_Matches (same fixtures). Only 2003-2011 (2793?) should remain + few 2012-2019 residue. 3847 = 6886 - 3039 removed. Expected novo survivors ≈ 2793 (2003-2011) + residue. So ~1000 novo 2012-2019 fixtures SURVIVED dedup against Brasileirao_Matches. Why? Fixture key = (comp, season, home, away, hg, ag) — mismatch on SCORE between the two files for those matches? Or home/away swapped? Let me check an example: find a novo 2019 match that also exists in Brasileirao_Matches with a different score.\n\nAND BRFB kept 847 in Série A (expected ~377 for 2023 + residue) — 470 residue! These inflate stats (9184).\n\nRoot cause: score discrepancies between sources (or team-id mismatches). Let me examine samples.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b5c56de0013IwRRUE70Mmxpx","sessionID":"ses_fa4ccfc0bffexSFu2vIRQjobrF","messageID":"msg_05b5c0471001QYwCgsKUhlq0nj"}}
