de... count = times registered = rows containing it ≈ 420).\n- \"Fluminense\" (novo, BRFB, FIFA) → pid \"fluminense\" bare.\n- \"Fluminense-PI\" (Copa) → pid \"fluminense-pi\", count small (~6).\n\nDefault: most frequent state → \"rj\" ✓. So bare → \"fluminense-rj\"...\n\nBut survivors show \"fluminense-pi\"!! Unless... `DEFAULT_STATES` has no fluminense entry, frequency → let me recheck `_default_state_for`:\n\n```python\nfor pid, entry in self._provisional.items():\n    if pid.startswith(base + \"-\"):\n        suffix = pid.rsplit(\"-\", 1)[1]\n        if suffix in BRAZILIAN_STATES:\n            state_counts[suffix] += entry[\"count\"]\n```\n\n`pid.startswith(\"fluminense-\")` — \"fluminense-rj\" ✓ count 420ish; \"fluminense-pi\" ✓ count 6; **\"fluminense de feira-ba\"** ✓✓✓ ALSO STARTS WITH \"fluminense-\"!!! suffix = rsplit → \"ba\" → state_counts[\"ba\"] += count(\"fluminense de feira-ba\")!! Fluminense de Feira appears in Copa do Brasil a lot! If \"fluminense de feira-ba\" count > \"fluminense-rj\" count → default = \"ba\"?! But survivors show \"pi\"...\n\nHmm wait, that gives \"ba\" not \"pi\". Let me recheck: survivors are \"fluminense-pi\" — where does PI come from?? Let me look at `_default_state_for` again... suffix from \"fluminense de feira-ba\" is \"ba\". From \"fluminense-rj\" → \"rj\". From \"fluminense-pi\" → \"pi\". Counts: rj ~420, pi ~6, ba ~?\n\nHold on — maybe the frequency isn't what I think. In Phase 1, `name_to_pid[raw] = registry.register(raw)` on FIRST occurrence; subsequent occurrences call `registry.register(raw)` again which increments count ✓. So counts should be right.\n\nHmm wait — but what about DEFAULT_STATES: no \"fluminense\". Let me just print `reg._default_state_for(\"fluminense\")` and the provisional counts. Also check what raw name in novo maps to \"fluminense-pi\": novo rows for Fluminense bare → pid \"fluminense\" → remap → ??? The remap showed `{'fluminense': 'fluminense-rj'}`?! But matches show \"fluminense-pi\" for novo