{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788239334506,"sessionID":"ses_fa4ccfc0bffexSFu2vIRQjobrF","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_654ec2a3e8bd40d0b27b1cf6","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-7f4a851aa2e1/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalizer.py","newString":"def _strip_edge_fillers(base: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Iteratively drop filler tokens from both ends while a stem remains.\n\n    Trailing: \"EC Bahia\" never happens but \"Bahia EC\" does; leading: the\n    datasets write both \"EC Bahia\" and \"Bahia EC\". \"Sport\" is NOT filler -\n    it is Sport Recife's actual name.\n    \"\"\"\n    tokens = base.split()\n    while len(tokens) > 1 and (tokens[0] in FILLER_TOKENS or tokens[-1] in FILLER_TOKENS):\n        if tokens[-1] in FILLER_TOKENS:\n            tokens.pop()\n        else:\n            tokens.pop(0)\n    return \" \".join(tokens)","oldString":"def _strip_trailing_fillers(base: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Iteratively drop trailing filler tokens while a non-empty stem remains.\"\"\"\n    tokens = base.split()\n    while len(tokens) > 1 and tokens[-1] in FILLER_TOKENS:\n        tokens.pop()\n    return \" \".join(tokens)"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-7f4a851aa2e1/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalizer.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-7f4a851aa2e1/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalizer.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-7f4a851aa2e1/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalizer.py\n@@ -219,13 +219,21 @@\n     state: Optional[str] = None     # Brazilian federative unit, lowercase\n     foreign: Optional[str] = None   # foreign-country marker, lowercase\n \n \n-def _strip_trailing_fillers(base: str) -> str:\n-    \"\"\"Iteratively drop trailing filler tokens while a non-empty stem remains.\"\"\"\n+def _strip_edge_fillers(base: str) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Iteratively drop filler tokens from both ends while a stem remains.\n+\n+    Trailing: \"EC Bahia\" never happens but \"Bahia EC\" does; leading: the\n+    datasets write both \"EC Bahia\" and \"Bahia EC\". \"Sport\" is NOT filler -\n+    it is Sport Recife's actual name.\n+    \"\"\"\n     tokens = base.split()\n-    while len(tokens) > 1 and tokens[-1] in FILLER_TOKENS:\n-        tokens.pop()\n+    while len(tokens) > 1 and (tokens[0] in FILLER_TOKENS or tokens[-1] in FILLER_TOKENS):\n+        if tokens[-1] in FILLER_TOKENS:\n+            tokens.pop()\n+        else:\n+            tokens.pop(0)\n     return \" \".join(tokens)\n \n \n def parse_name(raw: str) -> ParsedName:\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-7f4a851aa2e1/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalizer.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-7f4a851aa2e1/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalizer.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-7f4a851aa2e1/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalizer.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-7f4a851aa2e1/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalizer.py\n@@ -219,13 +219,21 @@\n     state: Optional[str] = None     # Brazilian federative unit, lowercase\n     foreign: Optional[str] = None   # foreign-country marker, lowercase\n \n \n-def _strip_trailing_fillers(base: str) -> str:\n-    \"\"\"Iteratively drop trailing filler tokens while a non-empty stem remains.\"\"\"\n+def _strip_edge_fillers(base: str) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Iteratively drop filler tokens from both ends while a stem remains.\n+\n+    Trailing: \"EC Bahia\" never happens but \"Bahia EC\" does; leading: the\n+    datasets write both \"EC Bahia\" and \"Bahia EC\". \"Sport\" is NOT filler -\n+    it is Sport Recife's actual name.\n+    \"\"\"\n     tokens = base.split()\n-    while len(tokens) > 1 and tokens[-1] in FILLER_TOKENS:\n-        tokens.pop()\n+    while len(tokens) > 1 and (tokens[0] in FILLER_TOKENS or tokens[-1] in FILLER_TOKENS):\n+        if tokens[-1] in FILLER_TOKENS:\n+            tokens.pop()\n+        else:\n+            tokens.pop(0)\n     return \" \".join(tokens)\n \n \n def parse_name(raw: str) -> ParsedName:\n","additions":12,"deletions":4},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalizer.py","time":{"start":1788239334502,"end":1788239334504}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"FOUND THE ROOT BUG: `suffix in BRAZILIAN_STATES` is **False** for \"rj\" and \"pi\"! So `BRAZILIAN_STATES` doesn't contain \"rj\"/\"pi\"...\n\nLook at the definition:\n\n```python\nBRAZILIAN_STATES: frozenset[str] = frozenset(\n    \"AC AL AP AM BA CE DF ES GO MA MT MS MG PA PB PR PE PI RJ RN RS RO RR SC SP SE TO\".split()\n)\n```\n\n`frozenset(\"AC AL ...\".split())` — `.split()` returns the list of tokens ✓ so BRAZILIAN_STATES = {\"AC\", \"AL\", ...} — contains \"RJ\" uppercase! My suffix is **lowercase** \"rj\" (from pid \"fluminense-rj\" — pids are lowercase!). `\"rj\" in {\"AC\",...,\"RJ\",...}` → False!!!\n\nTHAT'S THE BUG! In `_default_state_for`, pid suffixes are lowercase but BRAZILIAN_STATES has uppercase entries. So state_counts is EMPTY → fallback: `list({s for s in self._by_base.get(base, {}) if s and not s.startswith(\"foreign:\")})[0]` — **set iteration order is arbitrary** (hash-based) → picked \"pi\" this run, \"rj\" another run! NON-DETERMINISTIC BEHAVIOR across runs (PYTHONHASHSEED affects str hashing!). That also explains why my earlier probe runs gave DIFFERENT results than the test runs (9184 vs 8868 matches — different bare Fluminense defaults across runs → different dedup effectiveness!).\n\nAlso \"EC Bahia\" leading-filler bug is real and separate.\n\nFixes:\n1. `_default_state_for`: compare case-insensitively — `suffix.upper() in BRAZILIAN_STATES` (pid suffix is lowercase; states uppercase).\n2. Leading filler strip in `parse_name` (strip fillers from both ends iteratively).\n3. Also make the no-count fallback deterministic (sorted).\n4. `_canonical_from_parsed` uses `parsed.state` (already lowercase) — fine.\n\nAlso — the `DEFAULT_STATES` override covers flamengo/santos/etc. — that's why those worked. Fluminense hit the broken frequency path.\n\nAdditionally, for determinism everywhere, seed-independent: fix _default_state_for fallback to sorted()[0].\n\nLet me also double check `_STATE_DASH_RE`/`_STATE_SPACE_RE` extract UPPERCASE states (original string, before lowercase) ✓ then `.lower()` applied ✓ so parsed.state is lowercase. In register: `pid = f\"{parsed.base}-{parsed.state}\"` → lowercase suffix ✓. And `self._by_base` keys: `parsed.state if not parsed.foreign else f\"foreign:{parsed.foreign}\"` — lowercase states. In finalize: ambiguous check `brazilian_states = {s for s in states if s and not s.startswith(\"foreign:\")}` — no membership check against BRAZILIAN_STATES → works ✓ (that's why ambiguity detection worked).\n\nFix now. Also add a leading-filler strip:\n\n```python\ndef _strip_trailing_fillers(base):\n    tokens = base.split()\n    while len(tokens) > 1 and (tokens[-1] in FILLER_TOKENS or tokens[0] in FILLER_TOKENS):\n        if tokens[-1] in FILLER_TOKENS: tokens.pop()\n        else: tokens.pop(0)\n    return \" \".join(tokens)\n```\n\nWait — \"EC Bahia\" → tokens [\"ec\",\"bahia\"] → leading \"ec\" popped → \"bahia\" ✓. \"Athletic Club MG\" → state extracted first (\"MG\") → base \"athletic club\" → trailing \"club\" → \"athletic\" ✓. \"SC Internacional\" → leading \"sc\" → \"internacional\" ✓. Hmm — but wait: \"SC\" is also... Palmeiras full name \"Sociedade Esportiva Palmeiras\" — not in data. OK.\n\nEdge: \"Sport Club do Recife\" — tokens [\"sport\",\"club\",\"do\",\"recife\"] — trailing \"recife\" not filler; leading \"sport\" NOT in fillers ✓ stays → alias handles ✓.\n\nEdge: \"A.s.a. - AL\" → parse: state AL ✓ base \"a.s.a.\" → regex `[^a-z0-9 ]` → \"a s a\" hmm → \"a s a\" tokens... fine, consistent.\n\nThen re-run and see counts change. The remaining question: with fluminense → rj correct, novo survivors 2012-2019 (38/season Fluminense games) will dedup correctly, and BRFB \"EC Bahia\" matches dedup too. Expected final: Série A deduped ≈ 8868 (matches my very first sweep run — which by luck had the right hash seed!).\n\nAlso fix the fluminense tests to expect \"fluminense-rj\"? WAIT — with the fix, bare Fluminense → default rj → id \"fluminense-rj\" — still suffixed because base IS ambiguous (rj+pi exist). So matches carry \"fluminense-rj\". Tests should expect \"fluminense-rj\". Hmm — but display name \"Fluminense\" ✓ (DISPLAY_NAMES has \"fluminense\": \"Fluminense\" — KEY MISMATCH! DISPLAY_NAMES keys use bare \"fluminense\" but canonical id is \"fluminense-rj\"!). Need to update DISPLAY_NAMES keys for ambiguous bases: fluminense → \"fluminense-rj\", internacional → \"internacional-rs\" (already there ✓), santos-sp ✓, flamengo-rj ✓, botafogo-rj ✓, atletico-* ✓, america-mg ✓, nautico-pe ✓, santa cruz-pe ✓, juventude-rs ✓, guarani-sp ✓, bragantino-sp ✓... So just add/replace \"fluminense\" → \"fluminense-rj\". Also check other ambiguous bases with display entries: \"operario-ms\"? not in DISPLAY_NAMES (fallback). \"comercial\", \"rio branco\"... fallback fine.\n\nAlso DERBIES list uses (\"flamengo-rj\", \"fluminense\") — must become \"fluminense-rj\"!! That's why \"Fla-Flu\" wasn't found in derbies 2023! Fix DERBIES entries: fluminense→fluminense-rj. Also \"fluminense\" in test expectations. And \"vitoria\" (Bahia) — base vitoria ambiguous? Earlier collision scan: vitoria NOT in collisions... but bare+suffix? _by_base[\"vitoria\"] = {None, \"ba\"} → 1 Brazilian state → unambiguous → id \"vitoria\" ✓ DERBIES (\"bahia\",\"vitoria\") fine.\n\n\"paysandu\"/\"remo\" — unambiguous ✓. \"coritiba\" ✓. \"ceara\"/\"fortaleza\" ✓. \"avai\"/\"figueirense\" ✓. \"sport\" ✓. \"atletico-pr\" ✓. \"goias\" ✓, \"atletico-go\" ✓. \"gremio\"/\"internacional-rs\" ✓. \"corinthians\"/\"palmeiras\"/\"sao paulo\" ✓. \"flamengo-rj\"/\"botafogo-rj\"/\"vasco\" ✓.\n\nFix list:\n1. normalizer.py: `_default_state_for` case bug + deterministic fallback + leading filler strip + DISPLAY_NAMES \"fluminense-rj\" + DERBIES \"fluminense-rj\".\n2. tests: expect \"fluminense-rj\" (test_normalizer fuzzy test, test_match_queries pairing).\n3. test_server.py: `isError` → `is_error`.\n4. test_player_queries: Neymar potential 93 (not 92); club filter count for \"Santos\" — with \"ec bahia\" fix... wait why did club=\"Santos\" return 46? search_players(club=\"Santos\") does substring on club: \"santos\" in p.club.lower() → matches \"Santos\" AND \"Santos Laguna\" (26 players) = 46! My test expected exact 20. The substring behavior matches spec (\"Filter FIFA data by Club containing 'Flamengo'\") — substring is per spec! So adjust test: use exact-ish check or accept 46. Hmm — \"Santos\" substring is ambiguous with Santos Laguna. For the test, assert 46 (Santos 20 + Santos Laguna 26) or filter `club=\"Santos\"` expecting >= 20 and all contain \"santos\". I'll assert 46 with comment (spec says \"Club containing\"). Hmm — wait, actually earlier probe `svc.search_players(club=\"Santos\", limit=100)` — I predicted 20 but it's 46. And `club_squad(\"Santos\")` = 20 ✓ (uses fifa_clubs_by_team mapping — exact club strings). Both make sense. Update test.\n\nAlso test_sample_questions derbies count and stats numbers will change after the normalizer fix (stats: ~8868 — deterministic now). Let me recompute all ground truths after the fix, then update tests.\n\n5. test_competition_queries::test_season_coverage — what failed? Probably libertadores seasons: expected range(2013,2023) — the NA Libertadores row has season \"NA\" → to_int None → skipped ✓... but maybe the 2020 final recorded as 2020-01-30?? no wait — the row \"2020 2020-01-30 17:00:00 Palmeiras 1-0 Santos\" — season column says 2020 ✓. Hmm — actually the failure might be Copa do Brasil: expected range(2012,2024) = 2012..2023. Brazilian_Cup 2012-2021 + BRFB 2022-2023 ✓ = 12 seasons ✓. Or brasileirao range(2003,2024) = 21 seasons — with the EC Bahia fix... 2003-2023 ✓. Maybe the failure was caused by the hash-seed fluminense bug making some season shift? E.g. fluminense→pi meant... no, seasons come from season columns. Let me just rerun after fixes.\n\nAlso test_palmeiras_2023_stats (30-40 matches) — with EC Bahia fix, Palmeiras 2023 count changes (was inflated?). And test_palmeiras_overview 939 → will change (dedup now catches more).\n\nLet me apply the normalizer fixes now.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b5ecc5a0019i4aTG8E6DR0pl","sessionID":"ses_fa4ccfc0bffexSFu2vIRQjobrF","messageID":"msg_05b5dfdcc001I9z5S2Gu3ZM9Ur"}}
